window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 13 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000074981","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"A says: “B is the son of my father's only daughter.” How is A related to B? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A कहता है: “B मेरे पिता की एकमात्र पुत्री का पुत्र है।” A का B से क्या संबंध है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Father","hi":"पिता"},"2":{"en":"Cousin","hi":"चचेरा भाई"},"3":{"en":"Uncle","hi":"चाचा"},"4":{"en":"Cannot be determined","hi":"निर्धारित नहीं किया जा सकता"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"If A is a woman, A herself is the only daughter of her father and B is her son<br>If A is a man, the only daughter is A's sister and A is B's maternal uncle<br>As A's gender is not given, the relation cannot be determined<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Cannot be determined.</b>","hi":"यदि A स्त्री है, तो वही अपने पिता की एकमात्र पुत्री है और B उसका पुत्र है<br>यदि A पुरुष है, तो एकमात्र पुत्री A की बहन है और A, B का मामा है<br>A का लिंग नहीं दिया गया, अतः संबंध निर्धारित नहीं किया जा सकता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): निर्धारित नहीं किया जा सकता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000074982","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Which of the following numbers will replace the question mark (?) in the given series?<br>5, 31, 161, 811, ? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी संख्या दी गई श्रेणी में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर आएगी?<br>5, 31, 161, 811, ? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3450"},"2":{"en":"4061"},"3":{"en":"3870"},"4":{"en":"4456"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Each term is the previous term multiplied by 5 and then increased by 6<br>5 × 5 + 6 = 31, 31 × 5 + 6 = 161, 161 × 5 + 6 = 811<br>Next = 811 × 5 + 6 = 4061<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4061.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद पिछले पद का 5 गुना करके 6 जोड़ने पर मिलता है<br>5 × 5 + 6 = 31, 31 × 5 + 6 = 161, 161 × 5 + 6 = 811<br>अगला = 811 × 5 + 6 = 4061<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4061 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000074983","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"If in the word KEYBOARD the first and second letters are interchanged, in the same way the third and fourth, fifth and sixth and so on are interchanged, then what will be the 3rd letter from the right? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि शब्द KEYBOARD में पहले और दूसरे अक्षर को परस्पर बदला जाए, उसी प्रकार तीसरे और चौथे, पाँचवें और छठे आदि को बदला जाए, तो दाईं ओर से तीसरा अक्षर क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"D"},"2":{"en":"O"},"3":{"en":"A"},"4":{"en":"Y"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Pairs are swapped: KE → EK, YB → BY, OA → AO, RD → DR<br>New word = EK BY AO DR, i.e. EKBYAODR<br>Third letter from the right = O<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): O.</b>","hi":"युग्मों को बदलने पर: KE → EK, YB → BY, OA → AO, RD → DR<br>नया शब्द = EKBYAODR<br>दाईं ओर से तीसरा अक्षर = O<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): O है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000074984","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">27</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">42</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">27</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">42</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"42"},"2":{"en":"56"},"3":{"en":"64"},"4":{"en":"70"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In every row the third number is the first number multiplied by one less than the second<br>3 × (10 − 1) = 27 ✔ and 6 × (8 − 1) = 42 ✔<br>Missing number = 7 × (9 − 1) = 56<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 56.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में तीसरी संख्या = पहली संख्या × (दूसरी संख्या − 1)<br>3 × (10 − 1) = 27 ✔ तथा 6 × (8 − 1) = 42 ✔<br>लुप्त संख्या = 7 × (9 − 1) = 56<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 56 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000074985","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"Pointing to a portrait, a man says, \"The person in the portrait is the only grandson of the father of my wife's only brother.\" If the man has no siblings, how is the person in the portrait related to the man? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक चित्र की ओर संकेत करते हुए एक पुरुष कहता है, \"चित्र में दिख रहा व्यक्ति मेरी पत्नी के एकमात्र भाई के पिता का एकमात्र पौत्र है।\" यदि उस पुरुष के कोई भाई-बहन नहीं हैं, तो चित्र में दिख रहा व्यक्ति उस पुरुष से कैसे संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Son","hi":"पुत्र"},"2":{"en":"Nephew","hi":"भतीजा"},"3":{"en":"Cousin","hi":"चचेरा भाई"},"4":{"en":"Father","hi":"पिता"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Wife's only brother's father is the wife's father<br>His only grandson is the son of the wife's brother, since the wife is a daughter of the same father<br>So the boy is the son of the man's brother-in-law, i.e. his nephew<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"130\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 130\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M34 19H118M34 25H118\"/><path d=\"M220 28V55H220V78\"/><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Wife−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Wife−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Wife's brother+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Wife's brother+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Man+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Man+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Nephew+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Nephew+</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Nephew.</b>","hi":"पत्नी के एकमात्र भाई के पिता, पत्नी के पिता हैं<br>उनका एकमात्र पौत्र पत्नी के भाई का पुत्र है<br>अतः वह लड़का पुरुष के साले का पुत्र अर्थात उसका भतीजा है<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"130\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 130\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M34 19H118M34 25H118\"/><path d=\"M220 28V55H220V78\"/><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Wife−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Wife−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Wife's brother+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Wife's brother+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Man+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Man+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Nephew+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Nephew+</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): भतीजा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000074986","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">60</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">50</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">45</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">35</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">24</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">40</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">60</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">50</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">45</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">35</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">24</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">40</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25"},"2":{"en":"35"},"3":{"en":"45"},"4":{"en":"55"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In every row the third number is 5/9 of the sum of the first two numbers, rounded down<br>(30 + 60) × 5/9 = 50 ✔, (18 + 45) × 5/9 = 35 ✔, (12 + 25) × 5/9 = 20.55 → 20 ✔<br>Missing number = (24 + 40) × 5/9 = 35.55 → 35<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 35.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में तीसरी संख्या पहली दो संख्याओं के योग का 5/9 भाग है, जिसे नीचे की ओर पूर्णांकित किया गया है<br>(30 + 60) × 5/9 = 50 ✔, (18 + 45) × 5/9 = 35 ✔, (12 + 25) × 5/9 = 20.55 → 20 ✔<br>लुप्त संख्या = (24 + 40) × 5/9 = 35.55 → 35<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 35 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000074987","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"A is the male child of C. C and Q are sisters. Z is the mother of Q. P is the son of Z. Based on the given information, which of the following options is correct? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A, C का पुत्र है। C और Q बहनें हैं। Z, Q की माता है। P, Z का पुत्र है। दी गई जानकारी के आधार पर निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प सही है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"P is the maternal uncle of A.","hi":"P, A का मामा है।"},"2":{"en":"A and P are cousins.","hi":"A और P चचेरे भाई हैं।"},"3":{"en":"P is the brother of A.","hi":"P, A का भाई है।"},"4":{"en":"A is the paternal uncle of P.","hi":"A, P का चाचा है।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"C and Q are sisters and both are daughters of Z; P is the son of Z, so P is the brother of C<br>A is the son of C, hence P is the brother of A's mother → maternal uncle of A<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"196\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 196\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M28 28V55H28V78\"/><path d=\"M28 28V55H220V78\"/><path d=\"M28 28V55H124V78\"/><path d=\"M220 94V121H220V144\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Z−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Z−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A+</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): P is the maternal uncle of A..</b>","hi":"C और Q बहनें हैं तथा दोनों Z की पुत्रियाँ हैं; P, Z का पुत्र है, अतः P, C का भाई है<br>A, C का पुत्र है, अतः P, A की माता का भाई अर्थात A का मामा है<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"196\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 196\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M28 28V55H28V78\"/><path d=\"M28 28V55H220V78\"/><path d=\"M28 28V55H124V78\"/><path d=\"M220 94V121H220V144\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Z−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Z−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A+</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): P, A का मामा है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000074988","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Roll numbers are assigned such that the middle two digits represent the sum of the first two digits. Identify the invalid roll number. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रोल नंबर इस प्रकार दिए जाते हैं कि मध्य के दो अंक पहले दो अंकों का योग दर्शाते हैं। अमान्य रोल नंबर पहचानिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"381022"},"2":{"en":"450912"},"3":{"en":"720955"},"4":{"en":"661284"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"381022: 3 + 8 = 11 but the middle two digits read 10 ✘<br>450912: 4 + 5 = 9 and the middle digits are 09 ✔<br>720955: 7 + 2 = 9 and 09 ✔; 661284: 6 + 6 = 12 and 12 ✔<br>So 381022 is invalid<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 381022.</b>","hi":"381022: 3 + 8 = 11 परंतु मध्य के दो अंक 10 हैं ✘<br>450912: 4 + 5 = 9 तथा मध्य अंक 09 ✔<br>720955: 7 + 2 = 9 तथा 09 ✔; 661284: 6 + 6 = 12 तथा 12 ✔<br>अतः 381022 अमान्य है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 381022 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000074989","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>DEP, ZFL, VGH, ? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न अध्ययन कीजिए और अक्षरों का अगला समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>DEP, ZFL, VGH, ? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RHD"},"2":{"en":"RGD"},"3":{"en":"RHC"},"4":{"en":"RHE"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"First letters D, Z, V go 4 back, so next is R<br>Second letters E, F, G go 1 forward, so next is H<br>Third letters P, L, H go 4 back, so next is D<br>Next group = RHD<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): RHD.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर D, Z, V हर बार 4 पीछे, अतः अगला R<br>दूसरे अक्षर E, F, G हर बार 1 आगे, अतः अगला H<br>तीसरे अक्षर P, L, H हर बार 4 पीछे, अतः अगला D<br>अगला समूह = RHD<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): RHD है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000074990","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Select the odd number pair from the given alternatives. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से विषम संख्या युग्म चुनिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45, 2070"},"2":{"en":"38, 1482"},"3":{"en":"24, 600"},"4":{"en":"17, 308"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Second number = first number × (first number + 1)<br>45 × 46 = 2070 ✔, 38 × 39 = 1482 ✔, 24 × 25 = 600 ✔<br>17 × 18 = 306, not 308 ✘<br>So 17, 308 is the odd pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 17, 308.</b>","hi":"दूसरी संख्या = पहली संख्या × (पहली संख्या + 1)<br>45 × 46 = 2070 ✔, 38 × 39 = 1482 ✔, 24 × 25 = 600 ✔<br>17 × 18 = 306 है, 308 नहीं ✘<br>अतः विषम युग्म 17, 308 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 17, 308 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000074991","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Read the question carefully and choose the most appropriate option.<br>You are a school teacher. Two parents are arguing during a parent-teacher meeting and their disagreement is affecting the overall atmosphere. What would you do? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"प्रश्न को ध्यान से पढ़िए और सबसे उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br>आप एक विद्यालय शिक्षक हैं। अभिभावक-शिक्षक बैठक के दौरान दो अभिभावक बहस कर रहे हैं और उनका मतभेद समग्र वातावरण को प्रभावित कर रहा है। आप क्या करेंगे? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ask both parents to leave immediately without hearing their concerns.","hi":"दोनों अभिभावकों की बात सुने बिना उन्हें तुरंत बाहर जाने के लिए कहेंगे।"},"2":{"en":"Ignore the argument and continue the meeting as usual instead.","hi":"बहस को अनदेखा कर बैठक सामान्य रूप से जारी रखेंगे।"},"3":{"en":"End the meeting early and postpone all discussions indefinitely later.","hi":"बैठक जल्दी समाप्त कर सभी चर्चाएँ अनिश्चितकाल के लिए टाल देंगे।"},"4":{"en":"Listen to both sides calmly and help resolve the disagreement.","hi":"दोनों पक्षों को शांति से सुनेंगे और मतभेद सुलझाने में सहायता करेंगे।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A teacher's role is to keep the meeting calm and useful<br>Hearing both sides patiently and settling the matter restores the atmosphere<br>Removing, ignoring or postponing the parents solves nothing<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Listen to both sides calmly and help resolve the disagreement..</b>","hi":"शिक्षक का दायित्व बैठक को शांत और उपयोगी रखना है<br>दोनों पक्षों को धैर्य से सुनकर मामला सुलझाना वातावरण को सामान्य करता है<br>अभिभावकों को हटाना, अनदेखा करना या टालना समस्या का समाधान नहीं है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): दोनों पक्षों को शांति से सुनेंगे और मतभेद सुलझाने में सहायता करेंगे। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000074992","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Choose the best alternative.<br>◇1 : ◆3 :: ○2 : ? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सर्वोत्तम विकल्प चुनिए।<br>◇1 : ◆3 :: ○2 : ? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"◆4"},"2":{"en":"●5"},"3":{"en":"◆6"},"4":{"en":"●6"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In the pair ◇1 : ◆3 the hollow shape becomes the filled shape of the same kind and the number becomes three times itself, 1 → 3<br>Applying the same rule to ○2, the hollow circle becomes a filled circle and the number becomes 2 × 3 = 6<br>So the answer is the filled circle with 6<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ●6.</b>","hi":"युग्म ◇1 : ◆3 में खोखली आकृति उसी प्रकार की भरी हुई आकृति बन जाती है तथा संख्या तीन गुनी हो जाती है, 1 → 3<br>यही नियम ○2 पर लगाने से खोखला वृत्त भरा वृत्त बनता है और संख्या 2 × 3 = 6 हो जाती है<br>अतः उत्तर भरा हुआ वृत्त 6 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ●6 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000074993","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If L means '÷', M means '×', N means '+', and O means '-', which of the following statement(s) is/are NOT correct?<br><b>Statement I:</b> 40 L 8 N 10 M 2 = 25<br><b>Statement II:</b> 15 M 3 O 10 L 5 = 43 [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि L का अर्थ '÷', M का अर्थ '×', N का अर्थ '+' और O का अर्थ '-' है, तो निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा/से कथन सही नहीं है/हैं?<br><b>कथन I:</b> 40 L 8 N 10 M 2 = 25<br><b>कथन II:</b> 15 M 3 O 10 L 5 = 43 [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I","hi":"केवल I"},"2":{"en":"Only II","hi":"केवल II"},"3":{"en":"Both I and II","hi":"I और II दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither I nor II","hi":"न तो I और न ही II"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Statement I: 40 ÷ 8 + 10 × 2 = 5 + 20 = 25 ✔<br>Statement II: 15 × 3 − 10 ÷ 5 = 45 − 2 = 43 ✔<br>Both statements are correct, so neither is NOT correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither I nor II.</b>","hi":"कथन I: 40 ÷ 8 + 10 × 2 = 5 + 20 = 25 ✔<br>कथन II: 15 × 3 − 10 ÷ 5 = 45 − 2 = 43 ✔<br>दोनों कथन सही हैं, अतः कोई भी गलत नहीं है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो I और न ही II है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000074994","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of the question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br>A2C5E : B3D6F :: G8I11K : ? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>A2C5E : B3D6F :: G8I11K : ? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"H10J12L"},"2":{"en":"I9J12L"},"3":{"en":"H9K12L"},"4":{"en":"H9J12L"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Every letter moves one place forward and every number increases by 1: A→B, 2→3, C→D, 5→6, E→F<br>G8I11K gives H9J12L<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): H9J12L.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान आगे और प्रत्येक संख्या 1 बढ़ती है: A→B, 2→3, C→D, 5→6, E→F<br>G8I11K से H9J12L प्राप्त होता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): H9J12L है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000074995","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the given question, a few statements have been given followed by conclusions based on them. Consider the statements to be true and answer which of the given conclusions logically follow the statement.<br><b>Statements</b><br>1. Every nation that respects rights is democratic.<br>2. No authoritarian regime respects rights.<br>3. Country Z is not democratic.<br><b>Conclusions</b><br>I. Country Z does not respect rights.<br>II. Country Z is an authoritarian regime.<br>III. Some authoritarian regimes may become democratic.<br>IV. All democratic nations respect rights. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए प्रश्न में कुछ कथन और उनके आधार पर निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए और बताइए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-से तार्किक रूप से कथन का अनुसरण करते हैं।<br><b>कथन</b><br>1. अधिकारों का सम्मान करने वाला प्रत्येक राष्ट्र लोकतांत्रिक है।<br>2. कोई भी अधिनायकवादी शासन अधिकारों का सम्मान नहीं करता।<br>3. देश Z लोकतांत्रिक नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष</b><br>I. देश Z अधिकारों का सम्मान नहीं करता।<br>II. देश Z एक अधिनायकवादी शासन है।<br>III. कुछ अधिनायकवादी शासन लोकतांत्रिक हो सकते हैं।<br>IV. सभी लोकतांत्रिक राष्ट्र अधिकारों का सम्मान करते हैं। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I अनुसरण करता है"},"2":{"en":"Only I and II follow","hi":"केवल I और II अनुसरण करते हैं"},"3":{"en":"I and III follow","hi":"I और III अनुसरण करते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II अनुसरण करता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Respecting rights → democratic, so a non-democratic nation cannot respect rights; conclusion I follows<br>Not democratic does not force 'authoritarian regime', so II does not follow; III and IV are not supported<br>Only I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I follows.</b>","hi":"अधिकारों का सम्मान → लोकतांत्रिक, अतः गैर-लोकतांत्रिक राष्ट्र अधिकारों का सम्मान नहीं कर सकता; निष्कर्ष I अनुसरण करता है<br>गैर-लोकतांत्रिक होने से 'अधिनायकवादी शासन' अनिवार्य नहीं, अतः II तथा III, IV अनुसरण नहीं करते<br>केवल I अनुसरण करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I अनुसरण करता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000074996","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The government has increased investment in renewable energy to reduce dependence on fossil fuels.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Fossil fuels will be completely banned in the near future.<br>II. Renewable energy is considered important for the future. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों को देखिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा निष्कर्ष तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सरकार ने जीवाश्म ईंधन पर निर्भरता घटाने के लिए नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा में निवेश बढ़ाया है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. निकट भविष्य में जीवाश्म ईंधन पूर्णतः प्रतिबंधित कर दिए जाएँगे।<br>II. नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा को भविष्य के लिए महत्वपूर्ण माना गया है। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Investing more in renewable energy shows it is treated as important for the future, so II follows<br>A complete ban on fossil fuels is nowhere stated, so I does not follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only Conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा में अधिक निवेश दर्शाता है कि उसे भविष्य के लिए महत्वपूर्ण माना गया है, अतः II निकलता है<br>जीवाश्म ईंधन पर पूर्ण प्रतिबंध कहीं नहीं कहा गया, अतः I नहीं निकलता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000074997","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If '★' means +, '◆' means −, '○' means ×, and '△' means ÷, find [(18 △ 6) ◆ 2] ○ [(4 ★ 2) ○ 3]. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि '★' का अर्थ +, '◆' का अर्थ −, '○' का अर्थ × और '△' का अर्थ ÷ है, तो [(18 △ 6) ◆ 2] ○ [(4 ★ 2) ○ 3] का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12"},"2":{"en":"14"},"3":{"en":"16"},"4":{"en":"18"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"First bracket: (18 ÷ 6) − 2 = 3 − 2 = 1<br>Second bracket: (4 + 2) × 3 = 6 × 3 = 18<br>Now 1 × 18 = 18<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 18.</b>","hi":"पहला कोष्ठक: (18 ÷ 6) − 2 = 3 − 2 = 1<br>दूसरा कोष्ठक: (4 + 2) × 3 = 6 × 3 = 18<br>अब 1 × 18 = 18<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 18 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000074998","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the given conditions carefully and determine the appropriate outcome for the case provided. If any exception applies, identify the authority to whom the case should be referred.<br><b>Criteria for Industrial Safety Certification:</b><br>(i) Must have 3+ years of field experience.<br>(ii) Must have completed a certified safety course.<br><b>Exceptions:</b><br><b>Exception (A):</b> If field experience is exactly 2 years and the candidate is a mechanical engineer, refer the case to the Safety Director.<br><b>Exception (B):</b> If the candidate meets both criteria (i) and (ii) but has previously failed a safety inspection audit, refer the case to the Internal Audit Committee.<br><b>Case:</b> The candidate has 2 years of field experience, is a mechanical engineer, and has completed the certified safety course. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई शर्तों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और दिए गए मामले के लिए उपयुक्त परिणाम निर्धारित कीजिए। यदि कोई अपवाद लागू हो, तो वह प्राधिकारी पहचानिए जिसे मामला भेजा जाना चाहिए।<br><b>औद्योगिक सुरक्षा प्रमाणन के मानदंड:</b><br>(i) 3+ वर्ष का क्षेत्रीय अनुभव होना चाहिए।<br>(ii) प्रमाणित सुरक्षा पाठ्यक्रम पूरा होना चाहिए।<br><b>अपवाद:</b><br><b>अपवाद (A):</b> यदि क्षेत्रीय अनुभव ठीक 2 वर्ष है और अभ्यर्थी यांत्रिक अभियंता है, तो मामला सुरक्षा निदेशक को भेजें।<br><b>अपवाद (B):</b> यदि अभ्यर्थी दोनों मानदंड पूरा करता है परंतु पहले सुरक्षा निरीक्षण ऑडिट में असफल रहा है, तो मामला आंतरिक ऑडिट समिति को भेजें।<br><b>मामला:</b> अभ्यर्थी के पास 2 वर्ष का क्षेत्रीय अनुभव है, वह यांत्रिक अभियंता है और प्रमाणित सुरक्षा पाठ्यक्रम पूरा कर चुका है। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Certification to be approved","hi":"प्रमाणन स्वीकृत किया जाए"},"2":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Safety Director","hi":"मामला सुरक्षा निदेशक को भेजा जाए"},"3":{"en":"Application to be rejected","hi":"आवेदन अस्वीकार किया जाए"},"4":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Internal Audit Committee","hi":"मामला आंतरिक ऑडिट समिति को भेजा जाए"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Criterion (i) needs 3+ years, but the candidate has exactly 2 years and is a mechanical engineer<br>That fits Exception (A), so the case goes to the Safety Director<br>There is no failed audit, so Exception (B) does not apply<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Case to be referred to the Safety Director.</b>","hi":"मानदंड (i) में 3+ वर्ष चाहिए, परंतु अभ्यर्थी के पास ठीक 2 वर्ष का अनुभव है और वह यांत्रिक अभियंता है<br>यह अपवाद (A) में आता है, अतः मामला सुरक्षा निदेशक को भेजा जाए<br>कोई असफल ऑडिट नहीं है, अतः अपवाद (B) लागू नहीं होता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): मामला सुरक्षा निदेशक को भेजा जाए है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000074999","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"NUMBER\" is written as \"NvMcEs\" How will \"POCKET\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"NUMBER\" को \"NvMcEs\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"POCKET\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PpClEu"},"2":{"en":"PpClEv"},"3":{"en":"PqClEu"},"4":{"en":"PpCmEu"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Letters at odd places stay the same, even-placed letters move one place forward and become small caps: N-U-M-B-E-R → NvMcEs<br>POCKET: P, O → p, C, K → l, E, T → u<br>Code = PpClEu<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): PpClEu.</b>","hi":"विषम स्थान के अक्षर वही रहते हैं, सम स्थान के अक्षर एक आगे बढ़कर छोटे-बड़े रूप में आते हैं: N-U-M-B-E-R → NvMcEs<br>POCKET: P, O → p, C, K → l, E, T → u<br>कूट = PpClEu<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): PpClEu है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000075000","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question two statements are given and these statements are followed by two conclusions. You have to take the given two statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the two given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Some apples are fruits.<br>Some fruits are sweet.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All sweet are fruits.<br>II. Some sweet are fruits. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दो कथन और उनके बाद दो निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। दिए गए दोनों कथनों को सत्य मानना है, भले ही वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न प्रतीत हों। निष्कर्षों को पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा निष्कर्ष दिए गए दोनों कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कुछ सेब फल हैं।<br>कुछ फल मीठे हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी मीठे फल हैं।<br>II. कुछ मीठे फल हैं। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I अनुसरण करता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II अनुसरण करता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"'Some fruits are sweet' converts to 'some sweet are fruits', so II follows<br>'All sweet are fruits' is only a possibility, so I does not follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"'कुछ फल मीठे हैं' से 'कुछ मीठे फल हैं' प्राप्त होता है, अतः II अनुसरण करता है<br>'सभी मीठे फल हैं' केवल संभावना है, अतः I अनुसरण नहीं करता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000075001","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question, three statements are given followed by three conclusions. Consider the statements to be true even if they differ from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions carefully and decide which of the conclusions logically follow from the given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Some mangoes are fruits.<br>All fruits are foods.<br>No food is a liquid.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Some mangoes are foods.<br>II. All mangoes are foods.<br>III. Some foods are not liquids. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में तीन कथन और उनके बाद तीन निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न हों। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-से निष्कर्ष तार्किक रूप से अनुसरण करते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कुछ आम फल हैं।<br>सभी फल भोजन हैं।<br>कोई भोजन तरल नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कुछ आम भोजन हैं।<br>II. सभी आम भोजन हैं।<br>III. कुछ भोजन तरल नहीं हैं। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Both conclusions I and III follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और III दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"3":{"en":"All conclusions follow","hi":"सभी निष्कर्ष अनुसरण करते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Both conclusions II and III follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष II और III दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Those mangoes which are fruits are also foods, so I follows<br>'All mangoes are foods' is not certain, so II does not follow<br>No food is a liquid, so some foods are not liquids follows; conclusions I and III follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Both conclusions I and III follow.</b>","hi":"जो आम फल हैं वे भोजन भी हैं, अतः I अनुसरण करता है<br>'सभी आम भोजन हैं' निश्चित नहीं, अतः II अनुसरण नहीं करता<br>कोई भोजन तरल नहीं है, अतः कुछ भोजन तरल नहीं हैं निकलता है; निष्कर्ष I और III अनुसरण करते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): निष्कर्ष I और III दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000075002","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The municipal council should provide tax incentives to companies that adopt a four-day workweek to reduce overall energy consumption in office buildings.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. A four-day workweek will lead to a measurable reduction in energy usage in office environments.<br>II. Businesses are motivated by financial tax incentives to adjust their operational work schedules. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिया गया कथन ध्यान से पढ़िए और उस पर आधारित अनुमानों को देखिए। निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-से अनुमान कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>नगर परिषद को उन कंपनियों को कर प्रोत्साहन देना चाहिए जो कार्यालय भवनों में समग्र ऊर्जा खपत घटाने के लिए चार-दिवसीय कार्यसप्ताह अपनाएँ।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. चार-दिवसीय कार्यसप्ताह से कार्यालय वातावरण में ऊर्जा उपयोग में मापनीय कमी आएगी।<br>II. व्यवसाय अपने परिचालन कार्यक्रम बदलने के लिए वित्तीय कर प्रोत्साहनों से प्रेरित होते हैं। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The suggestion is made because a shorter week is expected to cut energy use, so I is implicit<br>Tax incentives are offered because businesses respond to them, so II is implicit<br>Both assumptions are implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Both Assumptions I and II are implicit.</b>","hi":"यह सुझाव इसलिए है क्योंकि छोटे कार्यसप्ताह से ऊर्जा खपत घटने की अपेक्षा है, अतः I निहित है<br>कर प्रोत्साहन इसलिए दिए जाते हैं क्योंकि व्यवसाय उन पर प्रतिक्रिया देते हैं, अतः II निहित है<br>दोनों अनुमान निहित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): अनुमान I और II दोनों निहित हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000075003","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"A visa-on-arrival is granted only if the traveler holds an eligible-country passport, has a return ticket, and shows funds of at least &#36; 500 — unless the traveler already holds a pre-approved e-visa, in which case it is granted regardless of the other conditions.<br><br>Traveler: eligible passport, return ticket present, funds shown &#36; 300, no e-visa. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वीज़ा-ऑन-अराइवल केवल तब दिया जाता है जब यात्री के पास पात्र देश का पासपोर्ट हो, वापसी टिकट हो और कम से कम &#36; 500 की राशि दिखाई गई हो — जब तक कि यात्री के पास पहले से अनुमोदित ई-वीज़ा न हो, जिस स्थिति में अन्य शर्तों के बावजूद वीज़ा दिया जाता है।<br><br>यात्री: पात्र पासपोर्ट, वापसी टिकट उपलब्ध, दिखाई गई राशि &#36; 300, ई-वीज़ा नहीं। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Visa granted","hi":"वीज़ा दिया जाए"},"2":{"en":"Visa granted with a funds bond","hi":"धन-बॉन्ड के साथ वीज़ा दिया जाए"},"3":{"en":"Referred to the immigration officer's discretion","hi":"आव्रजन अधिकारी के विवेक को भेजा जाए"},"4":{"en":"Visa denied","hi":"वीज़ा अस्वीकार किया जाए"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Passport and return ticket are in order, but the funds are &#36; 300 against the required &#36; 500<br>There is no pre-approved e-visa to override the condition<br>So the visa cannot be granted<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Visa denied.</b>","hi":"पासपोर्ट और वापसी टिकट ठीक हैं, परंतु राशि &#36; 300 है जबकि &#36; 500 आवश्यक है<br>शर्त को पूरा करने वाला पूर्व-अनुमोदित ई-वीज़ा नहीं है<br>अतः वीज़ा नहीं दिया जा सकता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): वीज़ा अस्वीकार किया जाए है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000075004","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)<br>Sericulture : Silk :: Apiculture : ? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है। (शब्दों को अर्थपूर्ण अंग्रेज़ी शब्द मानना है और उन्हें अक्षरों/व्यंजनों/स्वरों की संख्या के आधार पर एक-दूसरे से संबंधित नहीं मानना है।)<br>Sericulture : Silk :: Apiculture : ? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Leather","hi":"चमड़ा"},"2":{"en":"Wool","hi":"ऊन"},"3":{"en":"Milk","hi":"दूध"},"4":{"en":"Honey","hi":"शहद"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Sericulture is the rearing of silkworms for silk<br>Apiculture is bee-keeping for honey<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Honey.</b>","hi":"सेरीकल्चर रेशम के लिए रेशम कीट पालन है<br>एपीकल्चर शहद के लिए मधुमक्खी पालन है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): शहद है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000075005","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In each of the following questions, four options have been given, of which three are alike in some way and one is different. Choose the odd one out. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्नों में प्रत्येक में चार विकल्प दिए गए हैं, जिनमें तीन किसी प्रकार एक जैसे हैं और एक भिन्न है। विषम विकल्प चुनिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Canberra – Australia","hi":"कैनबरा – ऑस्ट्रेलिया"},"2":{"en":"Ottawa – Canada","hi":"ओटावा – कनाडा"},"3":{"en":"Washington, D.C. – USA","hi":"वाशिंगटन, डी.सी. – यूएसए"},"4":{"en":"Istanbul – Turkey","hi":"इस्तांबुल – तुर्किये"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Canberra, Ottawa and Washington, D.C. are the capitals of Australia, Canada and the USA<br>Istanbul is not the capital of Turkey; Ankara is<br>So Istanbul – Turkey is the odd pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Istanbul – Turkey.</b>","hi":"कैनबरा, ओटावा और वाशिंगटन डी.सी. क्रमशः ऑस्ट्रेलिया, कनाडा तथा अमेरिका की राजधानियाँ हैं<br>इस्तांबुल तुर्किये की राजधानी नहीं है; अंकारा है<br>अतः इस्तांबुल – तुर्किये विषम युग्म है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): इस्तांबुल – तुर्किये है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000075006","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"The \"PM Gati Shakti National Master Plan\" aims to bring together various infrastructure projects. Which of the following is a primary objective of this initiative? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\"पीएम गति शक्ति राष्ट्रीय मास्टर प्लान\" का उद्देश्य विभिन्न अवसंरचना परियोजनाओं को एक साथ लाना है। निम्नलिखित में से कौन इस पहल का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To promote renewable energy adoption across the country.","hi":"देश भर में नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा को अपनाने को बढ़ावा देना।"},"2":{"en":"To create a unified and integrated infrastructure development framework.","hi":"एकीकृत एवं समन्वित अवसंरचना विकास ढाँचा तैयार करना।"},"3":{"en":"To enhance digital connectivity in rural areas.","hi":"ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में डिजिटल कनेक्टिविटी बढ़ाना।"},"4":{"en":"To boost agricultural productivity through better irrigation facilities.","hi":"बेहतर सिंचाई सुविधाओं से कृषि उत्पादकता बढ़ाना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – To create a unified and integrated infrastructure development framework.</b><br>PM Gati Shakti is a <b>National Master Plan for multi-modal connectivity</b> that brings the infrastructure plans of sixteen ministries and all states on one GIS-based platform, so that a <b>unified and integrated infrastructure development framework</b> is created and projects avoid duplication and delays.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It was launched on <b>13 October 2021</b> by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry (DPIIT) with an outlay of ₹100 lakh crore.<br>• The plan covers economic zones, transport corridors, ports, airports, mass transit and logistics infrastructure mapped on a single portal.<br>• It is a \"whole of government\" approach that reduces cost overruns and helps in the <b>last-mile connectivity</b> of infrastructure projects.<br>• It complements the <b>National Logistics Policy (2022)</b> and the Bharatmala and Sagarmala programmes.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – एकीकृत एवं समन्वित अवसंरचना विकास ढाँचा तैयार करना।</b><br>पीएम गति शक्ति <b>बहु-मॉडल कनेक्टिविटी हेतु राष्ट्रीय मास्टर प्लान</b> है, जो सोलह मंत्रालयों तथा सभी राज्यों की अवसंरचना योजनाओं को एक GIS-आधारित मंच पर लाता है, जिससे <b>एकीकृत व समन्वित अवसंरचना विकास ढाँचा</b> बनता है और परियोजनाओं में दोहराव व विलंब टलते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसका शुभारंभ <b>13 अक्टूबर 2021</b> को वाणिज्य एवं उद्योग मंत्रालय (DPIIT) द्वारा ₹100 लाख करोड़ के परिव्यय के साथ हुआ।<br>• योजना में आर्थिक क्षेत्र, परिवहन कॉरिडोर, बंदरगाह, हवाई अड्डे, मास ट्रांज़िट तथा लॉजिस्टिक्स अवसंरचना एक ही पोर्टल पर मानचित्रित की जाती है।<br>• यह \"समग्र सरकार\" का दृष्टिकोण है, जो लागत-अतिक्रमण घटाता है तथा परियोजनाओं की <b>अंतिम-मील कनेक्टिविटी</b> में सहायक है।<br>• यह <b>राष्ट्रीय लॉजिस्टिक्स नीति (2022)</b> तथा भारतमाला व सागरमाला जैसे कार्यक्रमों का पूरक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000075007","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"The \"concept of 'One Nation, One Ration Card'\" is aimed at ensuring food security for migrant workers and their families. Which of the following technologies or systems is primarily used to facilitate the seamless implementation of this initiative across the country? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\"एक राष्ट्र, एक राशन कार्ड\" की अवधारणा प्रवासी श्रमिकों तथा उनके परिवारों की खाद्य सुरक्षा सुनिश्चित करना चाहती है। देश भर में इस पहल के निर्बाध क्रियान्वयन हेतु मुख्यतः कौन-सी तकनीक या प्रणाली प्रयुक्त होती है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Blockchain technology for tracking foodgrain distribution.","hi":"खाद्यान्न वितरण की निगरानी हेतु ब्लॉकचेन तकनीक।"},"2":{"en":"Biometric authentication through Aadhaar for beneficiary identification.","hi":"लाभार्थी पहचान हेतु आधार के माध्यम से बायोमेट्रिक प्रमाणीकरण।"},"3":{"en":"Satellite imagery for monitoring the movement of ration trucks.","hi":"राशन ट्रकों की गतिविधि की निगरानी हेतु उपग्रह इमेजरी।"},"4":{"en":"Mobile applications for online registration of beneficiaries.","hi":"लाभार्थियों के ऑनलाइन पंजीकरण हेतु मोबाइल एप्लिकेशन।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Biometric authentication through Aadhaar for beneficiary identification.</b><br>Under One Nation One Ration Card, a beneficiary can draw rations from any fair price shop in the country because the shop identifies the person through <b>biometric authentication linked to Aadhaar</b> on the electronic point of sale device. This Aadhaar-based biometric identification, together with the Integrated Management of Public Distribution System, allows portability of food entitlements.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• ONORC was launched in <b>2019</b> and implemented across all states and union territories by 2022 under the National Food Security Act, 2013.<br>• It benefits <b>migrant workers and their families</b>, who can lift their share of subsidised grain from any ePoS-enabled fair price shop.<br>• The scheme uses the <b>IM-PDS (Integrated Management of Public Distribution System)</b> portal, Aadhaar authentication and ePoS machines at fair price shops.<br>• The Public Distribution System covers about 80 crore beneficiaries under the NFSA; the Antyodaya and priority households get 5 kg per person per month.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – लाभार्थी पहचान हेतु आधार के माध्यम से बायोमेट्रिक प्रमाणीकरण।</b><br>एक राष्ट्र एक राशन कार्ड के अंतर्गत लाभार्थी देश के किसी भी उचित दर दुकान से राशन ले सकता है, क्योंकि दुकान इलेक्ट्रॉनिक पॉइंट ऑफ सेल उपकरण पर <b>आधार से जुड़े बायोमेट्रिक प्रमाणीकरण</b> द्वारा व्यक्ति की पहचान करती है। यही आधार-आधारित पहचान, IM-PDS के साथ मिलकर खाद्य अधिकारों को पोर्टेबल बनाती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ONORC <b>2019</b> में शुरू हुई और राष्ट्रीय खाद्य सुरक्षा अधिनियम, 2013 के अंतर्गत 2022 तक सभी राज्यों व केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों में लागू हुई।<br>• इससे <b>प्रवासी श्रमिक व उनके परिवार</b> लाभान्वित होते हैं, जो किसी भी ePoS-युक्त उचित दर दुकान से अपना रियायती अनाज ले सकते हैं।<br>• योजना में <b>IM-PDS पोर्टल</b>, आधार प्रमाणीकरण तथा उचित दर दुकानों पर ePoS मशीनें प्रयुक्त होती हैं।<br>• सार्वजनिक वितरण प्रणाली NFSA के अंतर्गत लगभग 80 करोड़ लाभार्थियों को समाहित करती है; अंत्योदय व प्राथमिकता परिवारों को प्रति व्यक्ति प्रति माह 5 किग्रा अनाज मिलता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000075008","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Who became the first Indian fencer to qualify for the Olympics? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"ओलंपिक हेतु अर्हता प्राप्त करने वाली पहली भारतीय तलवारबाज़ कौन बनीं? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bhavani Devi","hi":"भवानी देवी"},"2":{"en":"Mary Kom","hi":"मैरी कोम"},"3":{"en":"Dipa Karmakar","hi":"दीपा करमाकर"},"4":{"en":"Anshu Malik","hi":"अंशु मलिक"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Bhavani Devi</b><br><b>Bhavani Devi</b> (C.A. Bhavani Devi) became the first Indian fencer to qualify for the Olympic Games when she secured a place in the <b>sabre event at Tokyo 2020</b> through the Asian zonal qualification.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Bhavani Devi, from Tamil Nadu, won India’s first fencing gold at an international event at the <b>2017 Rehfuss Challenge</b> and is a multiple Asian Championship medallist.<br>• Fencing has three weapons — <b>foil, epee and sabre</b> — and the bout is played on a piste with electronic scoring.<br>• <b>Mary Kom</b> is a boxer, <b>Dipa Karmakar</b> a gymnast (first Indian woman gymnast at the Olympics) and <b>Anshu Malik</b> a wrestler.<br>• Bhavani Devi was supported by the GoSports Foundation and the Target Olympic Podium Scheme and received the Arjuna Award in 2020.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – भवानी देवी</b><br><b>भवानी देवी</b> (सी.ए. भवानी देवी) एशियाई क्षेत्रीय अर्हता के माध्यम से <b>टोक्यो 2020 के सेबर स्पर्धा</b> में स्थान पाकर ओलंपिक हेतु अर्हता प्राप्त करने वाली पहली भारतीय तलवारबाज़ बनीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• तमिलनाडु की भवानी देवी ने <b>2017 रेहफुस चैलेंज</b> में अंतर्राष्ट्रीय स्तर पर भारत का पहला तलवारबाज़ी स्वर्ण जीता और वे एशियाई चैंपियनशिप की अनेक पदक विजेता हैं।<br>• तलवारबाज़ी में तीन शस्त्र होते हैं — <b>फॉइल, एपी तथा सेबर</b> — और मुकाबला पिस्ट पर इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अंकन के साथ होता है।<br>• <b>मैरी कोम</b> मुक्केबाज़, <b>दीपा करमाकर</b> जिम्नास्ट (ओलंपिक में पहली भारतीय महिला जिम्नास्ट) तथा <b>अंशु मलिक</b> पहलवान हैं।<br>• भवानी देवी को गोस्पोर्ट्स फाउंडेशन व टारगेट ओलंपिक पोडियम योजना का सहयोग मिला तथा उन्हें 2020 में अर्जुन पुरस्कार मिला।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000075009","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which ancient Indian treatise extensively details the rules and strategies of traditional wrestling, known as Malla-yuddha? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा प्राचीन भारतीय ग्रंथ पारंपरिक कुश्ती, जिसे मल्ल-युद्ध कहा जाता है, के नियमों व रणनीतियों का विस्तार से वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Arthashastra","hi":"अर्थशास्त्र"},"2":{"en":"Manasollasa","hi":"मानसोल्लास"},"3":{"en":"Agni Purana","hi":"अग्नि पुराण"},"4":{"en":"Vishnu Purana","hi":"विष्णु पुराण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Manasollasa</b><br><b>Manasollasa</b> (Abhilashitartha Chintamani), an encyclopaedic work of the <b>Chalukya king Someshvara III</b> (12th century), gives a detailed account of <b>Malla-yuddha</b> — the traditional Indian wrestling — including its rules, training techniques and strategies.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Malla-yuddha is one of the oldest forms of Indian wrestling and is described in the <b>Mahabharata</b> (the duel of Bhima and Jarasandha) and in the Manasollasa.<br>• Someshvara III of the <b>Western Chalukya dynasty of Kalyani</b> wrote Manasollasa, a Sanskrit compendium dealing with governance, food, music, dance and sports.<br>• <b>Kautilya’s Arthashastra</b> deals with statecraft, economy and military strategy, while the <b>Agni Purana</b> and Vishnu Purana are religious texts containing genealogies and rituals.<br>• Later wrestling traditions include <b>Kushti and Pehlwani</b>, with the akhara as the training ground; Mallakhamb is a related gymnastic sport of Maharashtra and Madhya Pradesh.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मानसोल्लास</b><br><b>मानसोल्लास</b> (अभिलाषितार्थ चिंतामणि), <b>चालुक्य राजा सोमेश्वर तृतीय</b> (12वीं शताब्दी) का विश्वकोशीय ग्रंथ, <b>मल्ल-युद्ध</b> — पारंपरिक भारतीय कुश्ती — के नियमों, प्रशिक्षण तकनीकों व रणनीतियों का विस्तृत वर्णन करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मल्ल-युद्ध भारतीय कुश्ती का प्राचीनतम रूप है, जिसका वर्णन <b>महाभारत</b> (भीम-जरासंध का युद्ध) तथा मानसोल्लास में मिलता है।<br>• कल्याणी के <b>पश्चिमी चालुक्य वंश</b> के सोमेश्वर तृतीय ने मानसोल्लास लिखा, जो शासन, भोजन, संगीत, नृत्य व खेल पर संस्कृत संकलन है।<br>• <b>कौटिल्य का अर्थशास्त्र</b> राज्यशास्त्र, अर्थव्यवस्था व सैन्य रणनीति से संबंधित है, जबकि <b>अग्नि पुराण</b> व विष्णु पुराण वंशावली व कर्मकांड युक्त धार्मिक ग्रंथ हैं।<br>• परवर्ती कुश्ती परंपराओं में <b>कुश्ती व पहलवानी</b> आती हैं, जिनका प्रशिक्षण स्थल अखाड़ा है; मल्लखंभ महाराष्ट्र व मध्य प्रदेश का संबंधित जिम्नास्टिक खेल है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000075010","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In which city was the final of the <b>2011</b> Cricket World Cup contested? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>2011</b> क्रिकेट विश्व कप का फाइनल किस शहर में खेला गया? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mumbai","hi":"मुंबई"},"2":{"en":"Delhi","hi":"दिल्ली"},"3":{"en":"Kolkata","hi":"कोलकाता"},"4":{"en":"Chennai","hi":"चेन्नई"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Mumbai</b><br>The final of the 2011 ICC Cricket World Cup was played at the <b>Wankhede Stadium in Mumbai</b> on 2 April 2011, where India defeated Sri Lanka by 6 wickets to win the trophy after 28 years.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India co-hosted the 2011 World Cup with <b>Sri Lanka and Bangladesh</b>, and the tournament was won by India under M.S. Dhoni.<br>• <b>Yuvraj Singh</b> was adjudged Player of the Tournament and <b>Sachin Tendulkar</b> was playing his last World Cup; the winning six was hit by Dhoni.<br>• The Wankhede Stadium, owned by the Mumbai Cricket Association, was established in 1974 and has a capacity of about 33,000.<br>• India has won the Cricket World Cup twice — in <b>1983 at Lord’s</b> under Kapil Dev and in 2011 under M.S. Dhoni.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मुंबई</b><br>2011 आईसीसी क्रिकेट विश्व कप का फाइनल 2 अप्रैल 2011 को <b>मुंबई के वानखेड़े स्टेडियम</b> में खेला गया, जहाँ भारत ने श्रीलंका को 6 विकेट से हराकर 28 वर्षों बाद खिताब जीता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत ने 2011 विश्व कप की <b>श्रीलंका व बांग्लादेश</b> के साथ मेज़बानी की और एम.एस. धोनी की अगुवाई में खिताब जीता।<br>• <b>युवराज सिंह</b> को प्लेयर ऑफ द टूर्नामेंट चुना गया और <b>सचिन तेंडुलकर</b> का यह अंतिम विश्व कप था; विजयी छक्का धोनी ने लगाया।<br>• मुंबई क्रिकेट संघ के स्वामित्व वाला वानखेड़े स्टेडियम 1974 में बना और इसकी क्षमता लगभग 33,000 है।<br>• भारत ने क्रिकेट विश्व कप दो बार जीता — <b>1983 में लॉर्ड्स</b> पर कपिल देव के नेतृत्व में तथा 2011 में एम.एस. धोनी के नेतृत्व में।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000075011","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"During the first Five-Year Plan, which of the following most accurately represents the trade balance scenario? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"प्रथम पंचवर्षीय योजना के दौरान निम्नलिखित में से कौन व्यापार संतुलन की स्थिति का सर्वाधिक सटीक वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"India consistently maintained a trade surplus driven by robust export performance","hi":"सुदृढ़ निर्यात प्रदर्शन के कारण भारत ने लगातार व्यापार अधिशेष बनाए रखा"},"2":{"en":"Trade data is unavailable for this period","hi":"इस काल के लिए व्यापार आँकड़े उपलब्ध नहीं हैं"},"3":{"en":"The trade balance remained neutral, with exports and imports being roughly equal","hi":"व्यापार संतुलन तटस्थ रहा, निर्यात व आयात लगभग बराबर थे"},"4":{"en":"India generally experienced trade deficits due to large-scale imports for industrialization","hi":"औद्योगीकरण हेतु बड़े पैमाने पर आयात के कारण भारत सामान्यतः व्यापार घाटे का सामना करता रहा"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – India generally experienced trade deficits due to large-scale imports for industrialization</b><br>During the First Five-Year Plan (1951–56) India ran <b>chronic trade deficits</b>, mainly because of large imports of machinery, capital goods and foodgrains needed for industrialisation and to meet domestic shortages, while exports of primary commodities grew slowly.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The First Plan was based on the <b>Harrod–Domar model</b>, focused on agriculture, irrigation and power, and was financed largely by the sterling balances released after independence.<br>• The Second Plan (1956–61) adopted the <b>Mahalanobis model</b> and gave priority to heavy and basic industries, which increased capital goods imports and the deficit further.<br>• To manage the deficits, India used <b>import substitution, quotas and high tariffs</b>, and later sought foreign aid and PL-480 food imports.<br>• The <b>balance of payments crisis of 1957–58</b> forced the government to impose import controls and to approach the IMF and the World Bank.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – औद्योगीकरण हेतु बड़े पैमाने पर आयात के कारण भारत सामान्यतः व्यापार घाटे का सामना करता रहा</b><br>प्रथम पंचवर्षीय योजना (1951–56) के दौरान भारत का <b>व्यापार घाटा दीर्घकालिक</b> रहा, मुख्यतः औद्योगीकरण तथा घरेलू कमी पूरी करने हेतु मशीनरी, पूँजीगत वस्तुओं व खाद्यान्न के बड़े आयात के कारण, जबकि प्राथमिक वस्तुओं के निर्यात में धीमी वृद्धि हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रथम योजना <b>हैरोड–डोमर मॉडल</b> पर आधारित थी, जिसमें कृषि, सिंचाई व ऊर्जा पर बल था, और इसका वित्तपोषण मुख्यतः स्वतंत्रता के बाद मुक्त स्टर्लिंग बैलेंस से हुआ।<br>• द्वितीय योजना (1956–61) ने <b>महालनोबिस मॉडल</b> अपनाया और भारी व आधारभूत उद्योगों को प्राथमिकता दी, जिससे पूँजीगत वस्तुओं का आयात व घाटा और बढ़ा।<br>• घाटे के प्रबंधन हेतु भारत ने <b>आयात प्रतिस्थापन, कोटा व ऊँची दरें</b> अपनाईं और बाद में विदेशी सहायता तथा PL-480 खाद्य आयात का सहारा लिया।<br>• <b>1957–58 के भुगतान संतुलन संकट</b> ने सरकार को आयात नियंत्रण लगाने तथा IMF व विश्व बैंक से संपर्क करने पर विवश किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000075012","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"What does the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS), prescribe regarding \"mercy petitions\" in death sentence cases? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता (BNSS) मृत्युदंड के मामलों में \"दया याचिकाओं\" के संबंध में क्या प्रावधान करती है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"No mercy petitions allowed post-trial","hi":"विचारण के बाद कोई दया याचिका अनुमत नहीं"},"2":{"en":"The President alone decides without input from states","hi":"राज्यों के परामर्श के बिना केवल राष्ट्रपति निर्णय लेते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Multiple petitions allowed across jurisdictions","hi":"विभिन्न न्यायक्षेत्रों में अनेक याचिकाएँ अनुमत"},"4":{"en":"Clear timelines for filing and disposal","hi":"दायर करने व निपटाने हेतु स्पष्ट समय-सीमा"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Clear timelines for filing and disposal</b><br>The BNSS, 2023 prescribes <b>clear timelines</b> for mercy petitions in death sentence cases — the convict may file a petition within a fixed period, the state government must forward it with its comments within a specified time, and the President or Governor must decide it within a time limit. This is meant to end the indefinite delay that led to long delays in executions.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Under the BNSS, a death sentence must be <b>confirmed by the High Court</b>, and the convict has a right of appeal to the Supreme Court.<br>• The BNSS provides that a mercy petition must be disposed of by the President or Governor within a reasonable time, following the principle laid down in <b>Shatrughan Chauhan v. Union of India (2014)</b>.<br>• The BNSS replaced the <b>Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973</b> with effect from 1 July 2024, along with the BNS (IPC) and the BSA (Evidence Act).<br>• The new law also provides for time-bound investigation, trial and disposal of appeals, and mandates <b>video recording</b> of searches and seizures.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – दायर करने व निपटाने हेतु स्पष्ट समय-सीमा</b><br>BNSS, 2023 मृत्युदंड के मामलों में दया याचिकाओं हेतु <b>स्पष्ट समय-सीमा</b> निर्धारित करती है — दोषी निर्धारित अवधि में याचिका दायर कर सकता है, राज्य सरकार निर्धारित समय में अपनी टिप्पणी के साथ उसे अग्रेषित करेगी, तथा राष्ट्रपति या राज्यपाल को समय-सीमा में निर्णय लेना होगा। इसका उद्देश्य उस अनिश्चित विलंब को समाप्त करना है जिससे निष्पादन में बहुत देरी होती थी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BNSS के अनुसार मृत्युदंड की <b>उच्च न्यायालय द्वारा पुष्टि</b> आवश्यक है तथा दोषी को सर्वोच्च न्यायालय में अपील का अधिकार है।<br>• BNSS में प्रावधान है कि दया याचिका राष्ट्रपति या राज्यपाल द्वारा उचित समय में निपटाई जाए, जो <b>शत्रुघ्न चौहान बनाम भारत संघ (2014)</b> में स्थापित सिद्धांत पर आधारित है।<br>• BNSS ने 1 जुलाई 2024 से <b>दंड प्रक्रिया संहिता, 1973</b> का स्थान लिया, साथ ही BNS (IPC) तथा BSA (साक्ष्य अधिनियम) ने भी।<br>• नया कानून समयबद्ध अन्वेषण, विचारण व अपील निपटान का भी प्रावधान करता है तथा तलाशी व जब्ती की <b>वीडियो रिकॉर्डिंग</b> अनिवार्य करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000075013","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who was elected as the President of the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) in <b>2023</b>? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>2023</b> में अंतर-संसदीय संघ (IPU) के अध्यक्ष के रूप में किसे निर्वाचित किया गया? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Duarte Pacheco","hi":"डुआर्टे पाचेको"},"2":{"en":"Shirin Chaudhry","hi":"शिरीन चौधरी"},"3":{"en":"Tulia Ackson","hi":"तुलिया एकसन"},"4":{"en":"Om Birla","hi":"ओम बिरला"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Tulia Ackson</b><br><b>Tulia Ackson</b> of Tanzania was elected President of the Inter-Parliamentary Union in October 2023 at the 147th IPU Assembly in Luanda, Angola. She is the <b>31st President of the IPU</b> and the first woman from Africa to hold the post.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• She is the Speaker of the National Assembly of Tanzania and succeeded the Portuguese parliamentarian <b>Duarte Pacheco</b>.<br>• The IPU, founded in <b>1889</b>, is the global organisation of national parliaments, headquartered in <b>Geneva</b>, and works for peace, democracy and sustainable development.<br>• India is a founder member of the IPU; the IPU-India chapter is led by the Lok Sabha Speaker, and <b>Om Birla</b> has led Indian parliamentary delegations to IPU assemblies.<br>• The IPU organises the annual <b>Assembly of Women Parliamentarians</b>, and the 2023 assembly in Luanda had the theme of parliamentary action for peace and sustainable development.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – तुलिया एकसन</b><br>तंजानिया की <b>तुलिया एकसन</b> अक्टूबर 2023 में लुआंडा (अंगोला) की 147वीं IPU सभा में अंतर-संसदीय संघ की अध्यक्ष चुनी गईं। वे <b>IPU की 31वीं अध्यक्ष</b> तथा इस पद पर पहुँचने वाली अफ्रीका की पहली महिला हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वे तंजानिया की राष्ट्रीय विधानसभा की अध्यक्ष हैं और उन्होंने पुर्तगाली सांसद <b>डुआर्टे पाचेको</b> का स्थान लिया।<br>• <b>1889</b> में स्थापित IPU राष्ट्रीय संसदों का वैश्विक संगठन है, जिसका मुख्यालय <b>जेनेवा</b> में है और जो शांति, लोकतंत्र व सतत विकास हेतु कार्य करता है।<br>• भारत IPU का संस्थापक सदस्य है; IPU-भारत शाखा का नेतृत्व लोकसभा अध्यक्ष करते हैं तथा <b>ओम बिरला</b> ने IPU सभाओं में भारतीय संसदीय प्रतिनिधिमंडलों का नेतृत्व किया है।<br>• IPU वार्षिक <b>महिला सांसदों की सभा</b> आयोजित करता है; लुआंडा की 2023 सभा का विषय शांति व सतत विकास हेतु संसदीय कार्रवाई था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000075014","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Who among the following is the author of the Sanskrit play Mudrarakshasa? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से संस्कृत नाटक मुद्राराक्षस के रचनाकार कौन हैं? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Kalidasa","hi":"कालिदास"},"2":{"en":"Banabhatta","hi":"बाणभट्ट"},"3":{"en":"Vishakadatta","hi":"विशाखदत्त"},"4":{"en":"Brihatratha","hi":"बृहद्रथ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Vishakadatta</b><br><b>Mudrarakshasa</b> (\"The Signet Ring of Rakshasa\") is a Sanskrit play by <b>Vishakadatta</b>. It deals with the political machinations of Chanakya that helped <b>Chandragupta Maurya</b> to defeat the Nanda dynasty and secure the loyalty of Rakshasa, the Nanda minister.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Vishakadatta is also the author of <b>Devichandraguptam</b>; his plays are known for political realism and intrigue rather than romance.<br>• Mudrarakshasa is a source for Mauryan history and shows the practical application of <b>Kautilyan statecraft</b> — diplomacy, espionage and reconciliation of opponents.<br>• <b>Kalidasa</b> wrote Abhijnanashakuntalam, Malavikagnimitram and Meghaduta, while <b>Banabhatta</b> wrote <b>Harshacharita</b> and Kadambari.<br>• Other historical Sanskrit plays include <b>Mudrarakshasa</b>, Bhasa’s Svapnavasavadatta, Visakhadatta’s Devichandraguptam and Bhavabhuti’s Uttararamacharita.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – विशाखदत्त</b><br><b>मुद्राराक्षस</b> (\"राक्षस की मुद्रिका\") <b>विशाखदत्त</b> का संस्कृत नाटक है। इसमें चाणक्य की उन राजनीतिक चालों का वर्णन है जिनके बल पर <b>चंद्रगुप्त मौर्य</b> ने नंद वंश को पराजित किया और नंद मंत्री राक्षस की निष्ठा प्राप्त की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• विशाखदत्त ने <b>देवीचंद्रगुप्तम</b> भी लिखा; उनके नाटकों में प्रेम-कथा की अपेक्षा राजनीतिक यथार्थवाद व षड्यंत्र है।<br>• मुद्राराक्षस मौर्य इतिहास का स्रोत है और <b>कौटिल्य राजनीति</b> — कूटनीति, गुप्तचरी व विरोधियों के साथ समझौते — का व्यावहारिक प्रयोग दर्शाता है।<br>• <b>कालिदास</b> ने अभिज्ञानशाकुंतलम, मालविकाग्निमित्र व मेघदूत लिखा, जबकि <b>बाणभट्ट</b> ने <b>हर्षचरित</b> व कादंबरी रची।<br>• अन्य ऐतिहासिक संस्कृत नाटकों में <b>मुद्राराक्षस</b>, भास का स्वप्नवासवदत्तम, विशाखदत्त का देवीचंद्रगुप्तम तथा भवभूति का उत्तररामचरित सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000075015","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Census","question":{"en":"The rapid growth phase of the Indian Population was lying between which of the following time periods? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय जनसंख्या की तीव्र वृद्धि का चरण निम्नलिखित में से किस कालावधि में रहा? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1901-1921"},"2":{"en":"1921-1951"},"3":{"en":"1951-1981"},"4":{"en":"1981-2001"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 1951-1981</b><br>The period <b>1951–1981</b> is called the phase of <b>rapid growth of the Indian population</b>, when death rates fell sharply after independence because of better health care and disease control, while birth rates stayed high. The population grew from about 36 crore in 1951 to 68 crore in 1981.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>1901–1921</b> is the phase of a \"stagnant or stationary population\" with very slow growth due to famines and epidemics.<br>• <b>1921–1951</b> is the phase of \"steady growth\", which began with the Great Divide of 1921 when the population started to increase consistently.<br>• After <b>1981</b>, the growth rate began to slow — a high-growth phase giving way to a declining trend, and India’s decadal growth rate in 2011 was 17.7%.<br>• India became the world’s most populous country in 2023 with over 142 crore people, and Census 2027 will be the first digital census of India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1951-1981</b><br><b>1951–1981</b> की अवधि <b>भारतीय जनसंख्या की तीव्र वृद्धि</b> का चरण कहलाती है, जब स्वतंत्रता के बाद बेहतर स्वास्थ्य सेवाओं व रोग नियंत्रण से मृत्यु दर तेजी से घटी, जबकि जन्म दर ऊँची रही। जनसंख्या 1951 के लगभग 36 करोड़ से बढ़कर 1981 में 68 करोड़ हो गई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>1901–1921</b> \"स्थिर जनसंख्या\" का चरण है, जिसमें अकाल व महामारियों के कारण वृद्धि बहुत धीमी रही।<br>• <b>1921–1951</b> \"स्थिर वृद्धि\" का चरण है, जो 1921 के महाविभाजन से आरंभ हुआ, जब जनसंख्या लगातार बढ़ने लगी।<br>• <b>1981</b> के बाद वृद्धि दर घटने लगी — उच्च वृद्धि का चरण कम होने लगा; 2011 में भारत की दशकीय वृद्धि दर 17.7% रही।<br>• भारत 2023 में 142 करोड़ से अधिक जनसंख्या के साथ विश्व का सर्वाधिक जनसंख्या वाला देश बना; जनगणना 2027 भारत की पहली डिजिटल जनगणना होगी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000075016","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which legislative authority was granted under the Regulating Act of 1773? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1773 के नियमन अधिनियम के अंतर्गत कौन-सी विधायी शक्ति प्रदान की गई? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only the Court of Directors could issue laws.","hi":"केवल निदेशक न्यायालय ही विधि जारी कर सकता था।"},"2":{"en":"Governor General and Council could make rules for Fort William.","hi":"गवर्नर जनरल व परिषद फोर्ट विलियम हेतु नियम बना सकते थे।"},"3":{"en":"Civil regulations could only be passed by the British Parliament.","hi":"सिविल विनियम केवल ब्रिटिश संसद द्वारा पारित हो सकते थे।"},"4":{"en":"Military laws required Crown approval.","hi":"सैन्य विधियों हेतु क्राउन की स्वीकृति आवश्यक थी।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Governor General and Council could make rules for Fort William.</b><br>The Regulating Act of 1773 empowered the <b>Governor-General and his Council at Fort William</b> (Warren Hastings was the first Governor-General) to make <b>rules, ordinances and regulations</b> for the good order and civil government of the Company’s territories, subject to registration with the Supreme Court.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Act of 1773 was the <b>first step by the British Parliament to control the East India Company’s Indian affairs</b> and changed the designation of the Governor of Bengal to Governor-General of Bengal.<br>• It established the <b>Supreme Court at Calcutta (1774)</b> with Sir Elijah Impey as the first Chief Justice, and provided for a Council of four members to assist the Governor-General.<br>• It prohibited the servants of the Company from engaging in <b>private trade</b> and accepting presents or bribes.<br>• The <b>Pitt’s India Act, 1784</b> followed, creating a Board of Control and distinguishing between the commercial and political functions of the Company.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – गवर्नर जनरल व परिषद फोर्ट विलियम हेतु नियम बना सकते थे।</b><br>1773 के नियमन अधिनियम ने <b>फोर्ट विलियम के गवर्नर-जनरल व उनकी परिषद</b> (प्रथम गवर्नर-जनरल वारेन हेस्टिंग्स) को कंपनी के क्षेत्रों में सुव्यवस्था व सिविल शासन हेतु <b>नियम, अध्यादेश व विनियम</b> बनाने की शक्ति दी, जो सर्वोच्च न्यायालय में पंजीकरण के अधीन थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 1773 का अधिनियम <b>ईस्ट इंडिया कंपनी के भारतीय मामलों पर ब्रिटिश संसद के नियंत्रण की पहली पहल</b> था और इसने बंगाल के गवर्नर के पदनाम को गवर्नर-जनरल ऑफ बंगाल किया।<br>• इसने <b>कलकत्ता में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय (1774)</b> स्थापित किया, जिसके प्रथम मुख्य न्यायाधीश सर एलिजा इम्पे थे, तथा गवर्नर-जनरल की सहायता हेतु चार सदस्यीय परिषद का प्रावधान किया।<br>• इसने कंपनी के कर्मचारियों को <b>निजी व्यापार</b> तथा उपहार या रिश्वत लेने से रोका।<br>• इसके बाद <b>पिट्स इंडिया अधिनियम, 1784</b> आया, जिसने नियंत्रण बोर्ड बनाया तथा कंपनी के वाणिज्यिक व राजनीतिक कार्यों को अलग किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000075017","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Supreme Court and High Court","question":{"en":"Which Article of the Indian Constitution prohibits Parliament from discussing the conduct of a Supreme Court or High Court judge in the discharge of their duties? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का कौन-सा अनुच्छेद संसद को सर्वोच्च न्यायालय या उच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीश के कर्तव्य-पालन के आचरण पर चर्चा करने से रोकता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 119","hi":"अनुच्छेद 119"},"2":{"en":"Article 120","hi":"अनुच्छेद 120"},"3":{"en":"Article 121","hi":"अनुच्छेद 121"},"4":{"en":"Article 122","hi":"अनुच्छेद 122"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Article 121</b><br><b>Article 121</b> provides that <b>no discussion shall take place in Parliament with respect to the conduct of any judge of the Supreme Court or of a High Court in the discharge of his duties</b>, except upon a motion for presenting an address to the President for the removal of the judge.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 119</b> deals with the procedure for the election of the Deputy Chairman of the Rajya Sabha, and <b>Article 120</b> with the language to be used in Parliament.<br>• <b>Article 122</b> bars courts from inquiring into the proceedings of Parliament and provides that parliamentary proceedings cannot be questioned on the ground of any irregularity of procedure.<br>• The provision protects <b>judicial independence</b> by keeping the conduct of judges out of political debate, while removal is possible only through the impeachment procedure under Articles 124 and 218.<br>• A judge of the Supreme Court or a High Court can be removed only for <b>proved misbehaviour or incapacity</b> by an address of both Houses supported by a special majority.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अनुच्छेद 121</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 121</b> का प्रावधान है कि संसद में <b>सर्वोच्च न्यायालय या उच्च न्यायालय के किसी न्यायाधीश के कर्तव्य-पालन के आचरण पर कोई चर्चा नहीं होगी</b>, सिवाय उस प्रस्ताव के जिसमें न्यायाधीश को हटाने हेतु राष्ट्रपति को अभिभाषण देने का प्रस्ताव हो।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 119</b> राज्यसभा के उपसभापति के निर्वाचन की प्रक्रिया तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 120</b> संसद में प्रयुक्त होने वाली भाषा से संबंधित है।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 122</b> न्यायालयों को संसद की कार्यवाही की जाँच से रोकता है और यह निर्धारित करता है कि कार्यवाही में प्रक्रियागत अनियमितता के आधार पर प्रश्न नहीं उठाया जा सकता।<br>• यह प्रावधान न्यायाधीशों के आचरण को राजनीतिक बहस से दूर रखकर <b>न्यायिक स्वतंत्रता</b> की रक्षा करता है, जबकि हटाना केवल अनुच्छेद 124 व 218 की महाभियोग प्रक्रिया से संभव है।<br>• सर्वोच्च न्यायालय या उच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीश को केवल <b>सिद्ध कदाचार या अक्षमता</b> पर दोनों सदनों के विशेष बहुमत से अभिभाषण द्वारा हटाया जा सकता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000075018","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Force and Laws of Motion","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank:<br>Kinetic friction is generally ______ than the maximum static friction. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रिक्त स्थान भरिए:<br>गतिज घर्षण सामान्यतः अधिकतम स्थैतिक घर्षण से ______ होता है। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"greater","hi":"अधिक"},"2":{"en":"equal","hi":"बराबर"},"3":{"en":"less","hi":"कम"},"4":{"en":"unrelated","hi":"असंबंधित"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – less</b><br>Kinetic friction is generally <b>less</b> than the limiting (maximum) value of static friction, because once a body starts moving, the surfaces do not get enough time to interlock and the contact area reduces.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Static friction is a <b>self-adjusting force</b> that increases up to a maximum value, called the limiting friction; it is greater than kinetic and rolling friction.<br>• The force of friction is given by \\(f = \\mu N\\), where μ is the coefficient of friction and N the normal reaction.<br>• The order of magnitude is <b>static friction > sliding (kinetic) friction > rolling friction</b>, which is why wheels are used for transport.<br>• Friction produces heat, causes wear and is reduced by lubricants, ball bearings and polishing of surfaces.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कम</b><br>गतिज घर्षण सामान्यतः स्थैतिक घर्षण के सीमांत (अधिकतम) मान से <b>कम</b> होता है, क्योंकि वस्तु गति में आने पर सतहों को परस्पर अंतःस्थापित होने का पर्याप्त समय नहीं मिलता और संपर्क क्षेत्र घट जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• स्थैतिक घर्षण एक <b>स्वतः समायोजित बल</b> है, जो अधिकतम मान तक बढ़ता है, जिसे सीमांत घर्षण कहते हैं; यह गतिज व लोटन घर्षण से अधिक होता है।<br>• घर्षण बल \\(f = \\mu N\\) से दिया जाता है, जहाँ μ घर्षण गुणांक तथा N अभिलंब प्रतिक्रिया है।<br>• परिमाण का क्रम है — <b>स्थैतिक घर्षण > फिसलन (गतिज) घर्षण > लोटन घर्षण</b>, इसी कारण परिवहन में पहिये प्रयुक्त होते हैं।<br>• घर्षण ऊष्मा उत्पन्न करता है, घिसाव लाता है और स्नेहक, बॉल बेयरिंग तथा सतहों की पॉलिश से घटाया जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000075019","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"The <b>2025</b> International Booker Prize winner Banu Mushtaq wrote her original work in which language? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>2025</b> का अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार जीतने वाली बानू मुश्ताक ने अपनी मूल कृति किस भाषा में लिखी? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Malayalam","hi":"मलयालम"},"2":{"en":"Kannada","hi":"कन्नड़"},"3":{"en":"Telugu","hi":"तेलुगु"},"4":{"en":"Marathi","hi":"मराठी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Kannada</b><br><b>Banu Mushtaq</b> wrote the stories collected in <i>Heart Lamp</i>, which won the 2025 International Booker Prize, in <b>Kannada</b>. Deepa Bhasthi translated the work into English, and the author and translator shared the £50,000 prize.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <i>Heart Lamp</i> is a collection of twelve short stories drawn from three decades of Banu Mushtaq’s writing on the lives of Muslim women.<br>• Banu Mushtaq is a Kannada writer, lawyer and activist based in Karnataka; this was the first Kannada work to win the International Booker.<br>• The <b>International Booker Prize</b> is given annually for a book translated into English and published in the UK or Ireland; the author and translator share the award.<br>• In 2022 the prize went to <b>Geetanjali Shree</b> (Hindi) for <i>Tomb of Sand</i>, translated by Daisy Rockwell.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कन्नड़</b><br><b>बानू मुश्ताक</b> ने <i>हार्ट लैंप</i> में संकलित कहानियाँ, जिसने 2025 का अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार जीता, <b>कन्नड़</b> में लिखीं। दीपा भास्थी ने उनका अंग्रेज़ी में अनुवाद किया तथा लेखिका व अनुवादक ने £50,000 का पुरस्कार साझा किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <i>हार्ट लैंप</i> बानू मुश्ताक के तीन दशकों के लेखन से चुनी गई बारह कहानियों का संग्रह है, जो मुस्लिम महिलाओं के जीवन पर केंद्रित हैं।<br>• बानू मुश्ताक कर्नाटक की कन्नड़ लेखिका, अधिवक्ता व कार्यकर्ता हैं; अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर जीतने वाली यह पहली कन्नड़ कृति थी।<br>• <b>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार</b> प्रतिवर्ष अंग्रेज़ी में अनूदित तथा ब्रिटेन या आयरलैंड में प्रकाशित पुस्तक हेतु दिया जाता है; लेखक व अनुवादक पुरस्कार साझा करते हैं।<br>• 2022 में यह पुरस्कार <b>गीतांजलि श्री</b> (हिंदी) को <i>टॉम्ब ऑफ सैंड</i> हेतु मिला था, जिसका अनुवाद डेज़ी रॉकवेल ने किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000075020","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Indus Valley Civilization","question":{"en":"What distinguishes the Harappan bronze female figurine from the steatite statue? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"हड़प्पाई कांस्य महिला मूर्तिका को स्टीटाइट प्रतिमा से क्या अलग करता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She wears detailed garments.","hi":"वह विस्तृत वस्त्र पहने है।"},"2":{"en":"She lacks any body jewellery.","hi":"उसके शरीर पर कोई आभूषण नहीं है।"},"3":{"en":"She has short hair fillets.","hi":"उसके बाल छोटे फीते से बँधे हैं।"},"4":{"en":"She is largely unclad.","hi":"वह अधिकांशतः वस्त्रहीन है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – She is largely unclad.</b><br>The famous Harappan <b>bronze female figurine</b>, the \"Dancing Girl\" of Mohenjo-daro, is shown <b>largely unclad</b>, wearing only a necklace and a number of bangles, with her left arm covered with bangles. The steatite statue of the \"priest-king\" (or the seated male figure) is draped in a shawl with a trefoil pattern.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The bronze Dancing Girl was made by the <b>lost-wax (cire perdue) casting technique</b>, showing the Harappans’ skill in metallurgy and bronze casting.<br>• The steatite \"priest-king\" figure from Mohenjo-daro wears a shawl over the left shoulder and has a fillet around the head and a short beard.<br>• Other famous Harappan art includes the <b>bronze buffalo and bullock cart</b> figures, the bearded man in steatite and the terracotta Mother Goddess.<br>• Harappan artists used <b>bronze, terracotta, steatite, shell and faience</b>; the Dancing Girl is displayed in the National Museum, New Delhi.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – वह अधिकांशतः वस्त्रहीन है।</b><br>मोहनजोदड़ो की प्रसिद्ध हड़प्पाई <b>कांस्य महिला मूर्तिका</b>, \"नाचती हुई लड़की\", <b>अधिकांशतः वस्त्रहीन</b> दिखाई गई है — केवल हार व अनेक कंगन पहने, बायाँ हाथ कंगनों से भरा। \"पुजारी-राजा\" की स्टीटाइट प्रतिमा (अथवा बैठा पुरुष आकृति) त्रिपत्र अलंकरण वाले शोल पर आवृत है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कांस्य की नाचती लड़की <b>लॉस्ट-वैक्स (सिर पेर्दू) ढलाई तकनीक</b> से बनी, जो हड़प्पावासियों की धातुकर्म व कांस्य ढलाई में दक्षता दर्शाती है।<br>• मोहनजोदड़ो की स्टीटाइट \"पुजारी-राजा\" प्रतिमा बाएँ कंधे पर शोल पहने है तथा सिर पर फीता व छोटी दाढ़ी है।<br>• अन्य प्रसिद्ध हड़प्पाई कला में <b>कांस्य भैंसा व बैलगाड़ी</b>, स्टीटाइट का दाढ़ीधारी पुरुष तथा मृण्मयी मातृदेवी प्रतिमा सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• हड़प्पाई कलाकार <b>कांस्य, मृण्मयी मिट्टी, स्टीटाइट, शंख व फ़ाइंस</b> प्रयोग करते थे; नाचती लड़की राष्ट्रीय संग्रहालय, नई दिल्ली में प्रदर्शित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000075021","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: World Map","question":{"en":"Among the following Indian Ocean island nations, which is located closest to the African coast? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित हिंद महासागरीय द्वीप राष्ट्रों में से कौन अफ्रीकी तट के सर्वाधिक निकट स्थित है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mauritius","hi":"मॉरीशस"},"2":{"en":"Maldives","hi":"मालदीव"},"3":{"en":"Seychelles","hi":"सेशेल्स"},"4":{"en":"Sri Lanka","hi":"श्रीलंका"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Seychelles</b><br><b>Seychelles</b> is the Indian Ocean island nation closest to the African mainland — its islands lie about <b>1,500 km east of the East African coast</b>, whereas Mauritius is about 2,000 km and the Maldives and Sri Lanka lie close to India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Seychelles is an archipelago of about <b>115 islands</b> with Victoria as its capital; it is a member of the Indian Ocean Rim Association and the Commonwealth.<br>• India has a close defence and maritime relationship with Seychelles and helped develop the <b>Assumption Island</b> project and the Agalega airstrip in Mauritius.<br>• <b>Mauritius</b> lies east of Madagascar, the <b>Maldives</b> south-west of India and <b>Sri Lanka</b> south of India across the Palk Strait.<br>• Island nations of the Indian Ocean are important for India’s <b>SAGAR</b> vision (Security and Growth for All in the Region) and for the blue economy.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सेशेल्स</b><br><b>सेशेल्स</b> अफ्रीकी मुख्य भूमि के सर्वाधिक निकट हिंद महासागरीय द्वीप राष्ट्र है — इसके द्वीप पूर्वी अफ्रीकी तट से लगभग <b>1,500 किमी पूर्व</b> हैं, जबकि मॉरीशस लगभग 2,000 किमी दूर है तथा मालदीव व श्रीलंका भारत के निकट हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सेशेल्स लगभग <b>115 द्वीपों</b> का द्वीपसमूह है, जिसकी राजधानी विक्टोरिया है; यह हिंद महासागर रिम संघ तथा राष्ट्रमंडल का सदस्य है।<br>• भारत के सेशेल्स के साथ घनिष्ठ रक्षा व समुद्री संबंध हैं तथा उसने <b>असम्प्शन द्वीप</b> परियोजना तथा मॉरीशस में अगालेगा हवाई पट्टी के विकास में सहयोग किया।<br>• <b>मॉरीशस</b> मेडागास्कर के पूर्व, <b>मालदीव</b> भारत के दक्षिण-पश्चिम तथा <b>श्रीलंका</b> पाक जलसंधि के पार भारत के दक्षिण में है।<br>• हिंद महासागर के द्वीप राष्ट्र भारत की <b>SAGAR</b> दृष्टि (क्षेत्र में सभी हेतु सुरक्षा व विकास) तथा नीली अर्थव्यवस्था हेतु महत्वपूर्ण हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000075022","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A Judicial Magistrate of First Class (JMFC) sentences an accused to three years’ imprisonment (the maximum within his sentencing power) and a fine of ₹50,000. In default of payment of the fine, the court further directs that the accused shall undergo one year of imprisonment. Which of the following is most accurate under the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक प्रथम श्रेणी न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट (JMFC) अभियुक्त को तीन वर्ष कारावास (उसकी दंड देने की शक्ति की अधिकतम सीमा) तथा ₹50,000 जुर्माने का दंड देता है। जुर्माना न देने पर न्यायालय यह भी निर्देश देता है कि अभियुक्त को एक वर्ष कारावास भुगतना होगा। भारत में भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन सर्वाधिक सटीक है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Valid, because default imprisonment is separate from substantive punishment.","hi":"वैध, क्योंकि जुर्माना न देने पर कारावास मूल दंड से अलग है।"},"2":{"en":"Invalid, because default imprisonment cannot exceed one-fourth of substantive imprisonment competence.","hi":"अवैध, क्योंकि जुर्माना न देने पर कारावास मूल कारावास की दंड-शक्ति के एक-चौथाई से अधिक नहीं हो सकता।"},"3":{"en":"Invalid, because a Magistrate First Class cannot award imprisonment once maximum substantive imprisonment is imposed.","hi":"अवैध, क्योंकि प्रथम श्रेणी मजिस्ट्रेट अधिकतम मूल कारावास देने के बाद कारावास नहीं दे सकता।"},"4":{"en":"Valid only if approved by the Sessions Court.","hi":"वैध केवल यदि सत्र न्यायालय से अनुमोदित हो।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Invalid, because default imprisonment cannot exceed one-fourth of substantive imprisonment competence.</b><br>Under Section 30 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (formerly Section 65 of the CrPC), the <b>imprisonment in default of a fine cannot exceed one-fourth of the term of imprisonment</b> which the court is competent to inflict as punishment for the offence. Here the JMFC is competent to award up to three years, so the default imprisonment could not exceed nine months; a direction of one year is therefore invalid.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Where a court awards both imprisonment and fine, the <b>sentence in default of fine is in addition to</b> the substantive sentence, and it cannot be imposed without awarding a substantive sentence.<br>• A JMFC can award imprisonment up to <b>three years</b> and a fine up to ₹1 lakh under the BNSS.<br>• The Supreme Court in <b>Shantilal v. State of M.P.</b> held that default imprisonment cannot exceed one-fourth of the maximum substantive sentence.<br>• Section 65 of the CrPC has been re-enacted as <b>Section 30 of the BNSS</b>, with the same one-fourth limit retained.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अवैध, क्योंकि जुर्माना न देने पर कारावास मूल कारावास की दंड-शक्ति के एक-चौथाई से अधिक नहीं हो सकता।</b><br>भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2023 की धारा 30 (पूर्व में CrPC की धारा 65) के अनुसार <b>जुर्माना न देने पर कारावास उस कारावास की अवधि के एक-चौथाई से अधिक नहीं हो सकता</b> जिसे न्यायालय उस अपराध हेतु दंड के रूप में देने हेतु सक्षम है। यहाँ JMFC तीन वर्ष तक दे सकता है, अतः जुर्माना-कारावास नौ माह से अधिक नहीं हो सकता; एक वर्ष का निर्देश अतः अवैध है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• जब न्यायालय कारावास व जुर्माना दोनों देता है, तो <b>जुर्माना न देने पर कारावास मूल दंड के अतिरिक्त</b> होता है और मूल दंड दिए बिना यह नहीं दिया जा सकता।<br>• BNSS के अंतर्गत JMFC <b>तीन वर्ष</b> तक कारावास तथा ₹1 लाख तक जुर्माना दे सकता है।<br>• सर्वोच्च न्यायालय ने <b>शांतिलाल बनाम मध्य प्रदेश राज्य</b> में अभिनिर्धारित किया कि जुर्माना-कारावास अधिकतम मूल दंड के एक-चौथाई से अधिक नहीं हो सकता।<br>• CrPC की धारा 65 को <b>BNSS की धारा 30</b> के रूप में पुनः अधिनियमित किया गया है, जिसमें एक-चौथाई की सीमा यथावत है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000075023","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Part 1 and Part 2 of the Constitution","question":{"en":"Under Article 3 of the Constitution of India, what is the time period within which the President must refer a Bill affecting the area, boundaries, or name of a State to the concerned State Legislature for its views? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के संविधान के अनुच्छेद 3 के अंतर्गत, किसी राज्य के क्षेत्र, सीमाओं या नाम को प्रभावित करने वाले विधेयक को राष्ट्रपति किस अवधि के भीतर संबंधित राज्य विधानमंडल को उसके विचार हेतु संदर्भित करेगा? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A constitutionally fixed period of six months","hi":"संवैधानिक रूप से निर्धारित छह माह की अवधि"},"2":{"en":"A period specified by Parliament","hi":"संसद द्वारा निर्धारित अवधि"},"3":{"en":"One session of the state legislature","hi":"राज्य विधानमंडल का एक सत्र"},"4":{"en":"Such a period as the president may specify","hi":"राष्ट्रपति द्वारा निर्धारित ऐसी अवधि"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Such a period as the president may specify</b><br>The proviso to <b>Article 3</b> requires that no Bill for the formation of new states, alteration of areas, boundaries or names of states shall be introduced in Parliament except on the recommendation of the President, and where the Bill affects a state, the President shall refer it to the concerned <b>State Legislature for its views within such period as he may specify</b>. The views of the state are not binding on Parliament.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Article 3 was used for the reorganisation of states such as the creation of Telangana (2014) and the abrogation of Article 370 in Jammu and Kashmir (2019).<br>• Articles <b>1 to 4</b> deal with the Union and its territory, and laws made under Article 3 are <b>not deemed to be an amendment of the Constitution</b> under Article 368.<br>• <b>Article 2</b> provides for the admission or establishment of new states, while Article 3 covers internal reorganisation of existing states.<br>• The States Reorganisation Act, 1956 was the largest such exercise, creating 14 states and 6 union territories on the recommendation of the Fazl Ali Commission.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – राष्ट्रपति द्वारा निर्धारित ऐसी अवधि</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 3</b> का परंतुक निर्धारित करता है कि नए राज्यों के निर्माण, क्षेत्रों, सीमाओं या नामों के परिवर्तन का कोई विधेयक राष्ट्रपति की सिफारिश के बिना संसद में पुरःस्थापित नहीं होगा तथा जहाँ विधेयक किसी राज्य को प्रभावित करता है, वहाँ राष्ट्रपति उसे <b>राज्य विधानमंडल को उसके विचार हेतु ऐसी अवधि में संदर्भित करेगा जो वह निर्धारित करे</b>। राज्य के विचार संसद पर बाध्यकारी नहीं होते।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अनुच्छेद 3 का प्रयोग तेलंगाना के निर्माण (2014) तथा जम्मू-कश्मीर में अनुच्छेद 370 के निष्प्रभावन (2019) जैसे राज्य पुनर्गठनों में हुआ।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 1 से 4</b> संघ व उसके राज्यक्षेत्र से संबंधित हैं, तथा अनुच्छेद 3 के अंतर्गत बनी विधियाँ अनुच्छेद 368 के अंतर्गत <b>संविधान का संशोधन नहीं मानी जातीं</b>।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 2</b> नए राज्यों के प्रवेश या स्थापन का प्रावधान करता है, जबकि अनुच्छेद 3 वर्तमान राज्यों के आंतरिक पुनर्गठन से संबंधित है।<br>• राज्य पुनर्गठन अधिनियम, 1956 सबसे बड़ा ऐसा प्रयास था, जिसने फजल अली आयोग की सिफारिश पर 14 राज्य व 6 केंद्रशासित प्रदेश बनाए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000075024","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Under the economic reforms introduced since <b>1991</b>, which of the following pairs of Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs) has been granted Maharatna status? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>1991</b> से आरंभ किए गए आर्थिक सुधारों के अंतर्गत, निम्नलिखित में से केंद्रीय सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र उपक्रमों (CPSE) का कौन-सा युग्म महारत्न का दर्जा प्राप्त है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Indian Oil Corporation Limited and Steel Authority of India Limited","hi":"इंडियन ऑयल कॉर्पोरेशन लिमिटेड तथा स्टील अथॉरिटी ऑफ इंडिया लिमिटेड"},"2":{"en":"Hindustan Aeronautics Limited and Mahanagar Telephone Nigam Limited","hi":"हिंदुस्तान एरोनॉटिक्स लिमिटेड तथा महानगर टेलीफोन निगम लिमिटेड"},"3":{"en":"Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited and Airports Authority of India","hi":"भारत संचार निगम लिमिटेड तथा भारतीय विमानपत्तन प्राधिकरण"},"4":{"en":"Tourism Corporation Limited and Mahanagar Telephone Nigam Limited","hi":"टूरिज़्म कॉर्पोरेशन लिमिटेड तथा महानगर टेलीफोन निगम लिमिटेड"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Indian Oil Corporation Limited and Steel Authority of India Limited</b><br>Both <b>Indian Oil Corporation Limited</b> and <b>Steel Authority of India Limited</b> enjoy <b>Maharatna</b> status, which gives a CPSE greater financial autonomy — an investment ceiling of ₹5,000 crore in a single project without government approval.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Maharatna scheme was introduced in <b>2010</b>; other Maharatna companies include ONGC, NTPC, CIL, BHEL, GAIL, BPCL, HPCL, Power Grid and Hindustan Aeronautics (HAL).<br>• Maharatna status requires a Navratna company to have an average annual turnover of over ₹25,000 crore and a net profit of over ₹5,000 crore for three years.<br>• MTNL, BSNL, AAI and the Tourism Corporation are <b>not</b> Maharatna; only IOCL and SAIL in the given pairs qualify.<br>• The hierarchy of CPSEs is <b>Miniratna (Category I and II) → Navratna → Maharatna</b>, and the reforms of 1991 began disinvestment in these enterprises.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – इंडियन ऑयल कॉर्पोरेशन लिमिटेड तथा स्टील अथॉरिटी ऑफ इंडिया लिमिटेड</b><br><b>इंडियन ऑयल कॉर्पोरेशन लिमिटेड</b> तथा <b>स्टील अथॉरिटी ऑफ इंडिया लिमिटेड</b> दोनों को <b>महारत्न</b> का दर्जा प्राप्त है, जो CPSE को अधिक वित्तीय स्वायत्तता देता है — सरकारी अनुमोदन के बिना एक परियोजना में ₹5,000 करोड़ तक निवेश की सीमा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• महारत्न योजना <b>2010</b> में शुरू हुई; अन्य महारत्न कंपनियों में ONGC, NTPC, CIL, BHEL, GAIL, BPCL, HPCL, पावर ग्रिड तथा हिंदुस्तान एरोनॉटिक्स (HAL) सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• महारत्न दर्जे हेतु नवरत्न कंपनी का तीन वर्ष का औसत वार्षिक कारोबार ₹25,000 करोड़ तथा शुद्ध लाभ ₹5,000 करोड़ से अधिक होना चाहिए।<br>• MTNL, BSNL, AAI व टूरिज़्म कॉर्पोरेशन महारत्न <b>नहीं</b> हैं; दिए युग्मों में केवल IOCL व SAIL इस शर्त को पूरा करते हैं।<br>• CPSE का क्रम है — <b>मिनीरत्न (श्रेणी I व II) → नवरत्न → महारत्न</b>, और 1991 के सुधारों से इन उपक्रमों में विनिवेश आरंभ हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000075025","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which of the following was the primary stabilisation measures taken under the New Economic Policy (NEP) of <b>1991</b>? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>1991</b> की नई आर्थिक नीति (NEP) के अंतर्गत लिए गए प्राथमिक स्थिरीकरण उपाय कौन-से थे? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Long-term measures to improve efficiency","hi":"दक्षता सुधारने हेतु दीर्घकालिक उपाय"},"2":{"en":"Short-term measures to control inflation","hi":"मुद्रास्फीति नियंत्रित करने हेतु अल्पकालिक उपाय"},"3":{"en":"Measures to increase international competitiveness","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय प्रतिस्पर्धात्मकता बढ़ाने के उपाय"},"4":{"en":"Measures to remove rigidities in the economy","hi":"अर्थव्यवस्था की कठोरताएँ हटाने के उपाय"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Short-term measures to control inflation</b><br>The New Economic Policy of 1991 had two components — <b>stabilisation</b>, which consisted of <b>short-term measures to control inflation and correct the balance-of-payments deficit</b>, and <b>structural adjustment</b>, which consisted of long-term measures to improve efficiency and remove rigidities in the economy.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Stabilisation measures included <b>fiscal contraction</b> (cutting expenditure and subsidies), monetary tightening, devaluation of the rupee and measures to curb the fiscal deficit.<br>• Structural reforms included liberalisation of industry, the <b>New Industrial Policy of 1991</b> (abolition of licensing for most industries), trade liberalisation, financial sector reform and disinvestment.<br>• The crisis of 1991 was triggered by a balance-of-payments deficit, high inflation and low foreign exchange reserves of about <b>1 billion US dollars</b>, leading to IMF conditionalities.<br>• India devalued the rupee in <b>July 1991</b> and pledged gold to the Bank of England and the Bank of Japan to raise foreign exchange.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मुद्रास्फीति नियंत्रित करने हेतु अल्पकालिक उपाय</b><br>1991 की नई आर्थिक नीति के दो घटक थे — <b>स्थिरीकरण</b>, जिसमें <b>मुद्रास्फीति नियंत्रित करने तथा भुगतान संतुलन घाटा सुधारने हेतु अल्पकालिक उपाय</b> थे, तथा <b>संरचनात्मक समायोजन</b>, जिसमें दक्षता सुधारने व अर्थव्यवस्था की कठोरताएँ हटाने हेतु दीर्घकालिक उपाय थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• स्थिरीकरण उपायों में <b>राजकोषीय संकुचन</b> (व्यय व सब्सिडी में कमी), मौद्रिक कसाव, रुपये का अवमूल्यन तथा राजकोषीय घाटा घटाने के उपाय सम्मिलित थे।<br>• संरचनात्मक सुधारों में उद्योग का उदारीकरण, <b>1991 की नई औद्योगिक नीति</b> (अधिकांश उद्योगों के लाइसेंस की समाप्ति), व्यापार उदारीकरण, वित्तीय क्षेत्र सुधार व विनिवेश सम्मिलित थे।<br>• 1991 का संकट भुगतान संतुलन घाटे, उच्च मुद्रास्फीति तथा लगभग <b>1 बिलियन अमेरिकी डॉलर</b> के निम्न विदेशी मुद्रा भंडार से उत्पन्न हुआ, जिसने IMF की शर्तें लाईं।<br>• भारत ने <b>जुलाई 1991</b> में रुपये का अवमूल्यन किया तथा विदेशी मुद्रा जुटाने हेतु बैंक ऑफ इंग्लैंड व बैंक ऑफ जापान के पास सोना गिरवी रखा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000075026","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"Which dimension of Human Development Index (HDI) is most directly linked with longevity? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मानव विकास सूचकांक (HDI) का कौन-सा आयाम सर्वाधिक सीधे दीर्घायु से जुड़ा है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Knowledge","hi":"ज्ञान"},"2":{"en":"Income","hi":"आय"},"3":{"en":"Employment","hi":"रोजगार"},"4":{"en":"Health","hi":"स्वास्थ्य"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Health</b><br>In the Human Development Index, the health dimension is measured by <b>life expectancy at birth</b>, which is directly linked with <b>longevity</b>. The other two dimensions are knowledge (mean and expected years of schooling) and standard of living (GNI per capita).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The HDI has <b>three dimensions</b> — a long and healthy life, access to knowledge and a decent standard of living.<br>• It was developed by <b>Mahbub ul Haq</b> and Amartya Sen in 1990 and is published annually by the UNDP in the Human Development Report.<br>• HDI values range from <b>0 to 1</b>, and India’s HDI in the 2025 report placed it in the medium human development category.<br>• Related UNDP indices are the <b>Human Development Index, Inequality-adjusted HDI, Gender Development Index, Gender Inequality Index and Multidimensional Poverty Index</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – स्वास्थ्य</b><br>मानव विकास सूचकांक में स्वास्थ्य आयाम <b>जन्म के समय जीवन प्रत्याशा</b> से मापा जाता है, जो सीधे <b>दीर्घायु</b> से जुड़ा है। अन्य दो आयाम ज्ञान (स्कूली शिक्षा के औसत व प्रत्याशित वर्ष) तथा जीवन स्तर (प्रति व्यक्ति GNI) हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• HDI के <b>तीन आयाम</b> हैं — दीर्घ व स्वस्थ जीवन, ज्ञान तक पहुँच तथा सम्मानजनक जीवन स्तर।<br>• इसे <b>महबूब-उल-हक</b> व अमर्त्य सेन ने 1990 में विकसित किया और यह UNDP द्वारा मानव विकास रिपोर्ट में प्रतिवर्ष प्रकाशित होता है।<br>• HDI का मान <b>0 से 1</b> तक होता है; 2025 की रिपोर्ट में भारत मध्यम मानव विकास श्रेणी में है।<br>• UNDP के संबंधित सूचकांक हैं — <b>मानव विकास सूचकांक, असमानता-समायोजित HDI, लैंगिक विकास सूचकांक, लैंगिक असमानता सूचकांक तथा बहुआयामी गरीबी सूचकांक</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000075027","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"In the calculation of the Human Development Index (HDI), purchasing power parity (PPP) is primarily used to: [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मानव विकास सूचकांक (HDI) की गणना में क्रय शक्ति समता (PPP) मुख्यतः किस हेतु प्रयुक्त होती है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Compare income levels across countries after accounting for differences in the cost of living","hi":"जीवन-यापन लागत के अंतर का लेखा करने के बाद देशों के बीच आय स्तरों की तुलना करना"},"2":{"en":"Compare unemployment levels across countries after accounting for differences in labour-force participation","hi":"श्रम-बल भागीदारी के अंतर का लेखा करने के बाद देशों के बीच बेरोजगारी स्तरों की तुलना करना"},"3":{"en":"Compare population growth rates across countries after accounting for differences in demographic trends","hi":"जनसांख्यिकीय रुझानों के अंतर का लेखा करने के बाद देशों के बीच जनसंख्या वृद्धि दरों की तुलना करना"},"4":{"en":"Compare literacy levels across countries after accounting for differences in educational systems","hi":"शिक्षा प्रणालियों के अंतर का लेखा करने के बाद देशों के बीच साक्षरता स्तरों की तुलना करना"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Compare income levels across countries after accounting for differences in the cost of living</b><br>HDI uses <b>GNI per capita in purchasing power parity dollars</b> so that the income levels of different countries can be <b>compared after adjusting for differences in the cost of living</b> — for example, the same income buys more in India than in the United States.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• PPP is an exchange rate that equates the price of a basket of goods and services in different countries, so a dollar buys the same basket everywhere.<br>• HDI income is measured as <b>Gross National Income per capita in 2017 PPP terms</b>, transformed by a logarithmic formula to reflect diminishing returns of income.<br>• India’s PPP-based GDP makes it the <b>third largest economy in the world</b>, though in nominal terms it ranks lower.<br>• The World Bank uses PPP for international poverty comparisons, with the extreme poverty line at <b>2.15 PPP dollars</b> per person per day.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – जीवन-यापन लागत के अंतर का लेखा करने के बाद देशों के बीच आय स्तरों की तुलना करना</b><br>HDI में <b>क्रय शक्ति समता डॉलर में प्रति व्यक्ति GNI</b> प्रयुक्त होता है, जिससे विभिन्न देशों के आय स्तरों की तुलना <b>जीवन-यापन लागत के अंतर का समायोजन करके</b> की जा सके — उदाहरण के लिए, समान आय से भारत में अमेरिका की तुलना में अधिक वस्तुएँ मिलती हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• PPP वह विनिमय दर है जो विभिन्न देशों में वस्तुओं व सेवाओं की एक टोकरी के मूल्य को समान बनाती है, जिससे एक डॉलर सर्वत्र समान टोकरी खरीदता है।<br>• HDI में आय <b>प्रति व्यक्ति सकल राष्ट्रीय आय (2017 PPP डॉलर)</b> के रूप में मापी जाती है, जिसे आय के घटते प्रतिफल को दर्शाने हेतु लघुगणकीय सूत्र से रूपांतरित किया जाता है।<br>• PPP-आधारित GDP में भारत <b>विश्व की तीसरी सबसे बड़ी अर्थव्यवस्था</b> है, जबकि नाममात्र रूप में इसका स्थान नीचे है।<br>• विश्व बैंक अंतर्राष्ट्रीय गरीबी तुलना हेतु PPP का उपयोग करता है, जिसमें अत्यधिक गरीबी रेखा <b>2.15 PPP डॉलर</b> प्रति व्यक्ति प्रतिदिन है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000075028","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"What primary mandate was given to the Planning Commission of India upon its establishment in March 1950? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मार्च 1950 में स्थापना के समय भारत के योजना आयोग को कौन-सा प्राथमिक दायित्व दिया गया था? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Conducting national demographic census surveys","hi":"राष्ट्रीय जनसांख्यिकीय जनगणना सर्वेक्षण करना"},"2":{"en":"Managing direct foreign investment flows","hi":"प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी निवेश प्रवाह का प्रबंधन करना"},"3":{"en":"Formulating balanced national resource utilization","hi":"संतुलित राष्ट्रीय संसाधन उपयोग का प्रारूप तैयार करना"},"4":{"en":"Operating basic and heavy industries","hi":"आधारभूत व भारी उद्योगों का संचालन करना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Formulating balanced national resource utilization</b><br>The Planning Commission, set up in <b>March 1950</b> with the Prime Minister as its Chairman, was given the mandate of <b>formulating plans for the balanced utilisation of the country’s material, capital and human resources</b> and of preparing five-year plans.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Planning Commission was a <b>non-constitutional and non-statutory body</b>, created by a resolution of the Government of India; it was replaced by the <b>NITI Aayog</b> on 1 January 2015.<br>• Its functions included assessing resources, formulating plans, appraising progress and advising on economic policy; <b>P.C. Mahalanobis</b> was a key member and Jawaharlal Nehru the first Chairman.<br>• The <b>First Five-Year Plan (1951–56)</b> was based on the Harrod–Domar model and targeted agriculture and irrigation; the Second Plan adopted the Mahalanobis model.<br>• The <b>National Development Council (1952)</b> approved the plans, and the Planning Commission was a \"think tank\" rather than an operator of industries.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – संतुलित राष्ट्रीय संसाधन उपयोग का प्रारूप तैयार करना</b><br><b>मार्च 1950</b> में प्रधानमंत्री की अध्यक्षता में गठित योजना आयोग को <b>देश के भौतिक, पूँजीगत व मानव संसाधनों के संतुलित उपयोग हेतु योजनाएँ बनाने</b> तथा पंचवर्षीय योजनाएँ तैयार करने का दायित्व दिया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• योजना आयोग <b>गैर-संवैधानिक व गैर-सांविधिक</b> निकाय था, जिसे भारत सरकार के संकल्प से बनाया गया; 1 जनवरी 2015 को इसका स्थान <b>नीति आयोग</b> ने लिया।<br>• इसके कार्यों में संसाधनों का आकलन, योजना निर्माण, प्रगति का मूल्यांकन तथा आर्थिक नीति पर सलाह सम्मिलित थी; <b>पी.सी. महालनोबिस</b> प्रमुख सदस्य तथा जवाहरलाल नेहरू प्रथम अध्यक्ष थे।<br>• <b>प्रथम पंचवर्षीय योजना (1951–56)</b> हैरोड–डोमर मॉडल पर आधारित थी और कृषि व सिंचाई पर केंद्रित थी; द्वितीय योजना ने महालनोबिस मॉडल अपनाया।<br>• <b>राष्ट्रीय विकास परिषद (1952)</b> योजनाओं को स्वीकृति देती थी, तथा योजना आयोग उद्योगों का संचालक नहीं बल्कि \"थिंक टैंक\" था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000075029","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Socio Religious Reforms","question":{"en":"The Hindu Widows’ Remarriage Act was passed during the tenure of which Governor-General of India? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"हिंदू विधवा पुनर्विवाह अधिनियम भारत के किस गवर्नर-जनरल के कार्यकाल में पारित हुआ था? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lord Cornwallis","hi":"लॉर्ड कॉर्नवॉलिस"},"2":{"en":"Lord Canning","hi":"लॉर्ड कैनिंग"},"3":{"en":"Lord William Bentinck","hi":"लॉर्ड विलियम बेंटिक"},"4":{"en":"Lord Ripon","hi":"लॉर्ड रिपन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Lord Canning</b><br>The <b>Hindu Widows’ Remarriage Act, 1856</b> was passed during the tenure of <b>Lord Canning</b> (Governor-General 1856–62), largely due to the efforts of <b>Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar</b>. It legalised the remarriage of Hindu widows and protected their rights of inheritance.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Vidyasagar campaigned for widow remarriage and faced strong orthodox opposition; the Act was enacted on <b>26 July 1856</b>.<br>• The Act was later amended by the <b>Hindu Widows’ Remarriage (Repeal) Act, 1983</b>, and the Hindu Marriage Act, 1955 and the Hindu Succession Act, 1956 now govern such rights.<br>• <b>Lord William Bentinck</b> is associated with the abolition of Sati (1829) and the suppression of thuggee, with Raja Ram Mohan Roy’s support.<br>• Other social laws include the <b>Age of Consent Act (1891)</b>, the Sarda Act (1929) and the Abolition of Sati Acts of 1829.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – लॉर्ड कैनिंग</b><br><b>हिंदू विधवा पुनर्विवाह अधिनियम, 1856</b> <b>लॉर्ड कैनिंग</b> (गवर्नर-जनरल 1856–62) के कार्यकाल में मुख्यतः <b>ईश्वरचंद्र विद्यासागर</b> के प्रयासों से पारित हुआ। इसने हिंदू विधवाओं के पुनर्विवाह को विधिमान्य किया तथा उनके उत्तराधिकार अधिकारों की रक्षा की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• विद्यासागर ने विधवा पुनर्विवाह हेतु अभियान चलाया और कट्टर विरोध का सामना किया; अधिनियम <b>26 जुलाई 1856</b> को पारित हुआ।<br>• अधिनियम को बाद में <b>हिंदू विधवा पुनर्विवाह (निरसन) अधिनियम, 1983</b> से संशोधित किया गया तथा अब हिंदू विवाह अधिनियम, 1955 व हिंदू उत्तराधिकार अधिनियम, 1956 ये अधिकार नियंत्रित करते हैं।<br>• <b>लॉर्ड विलियम बेंटिक</b> का संबंध सती प्रथा के उन्मूलन (1829) तथा ठगी के दमन से है, जिसमें राजा राममोहन राय का सहयोग था।<br>• अन्य सामाजिक विधानों में <b>सहमति की आयु अधिनियम (1891)</b>, सारदा अधिनियम (1929) तथा 1829 के सती उन्मूलन अधिनियम सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000075030","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Diseases","question":{"en":"A vaccine may introduce weakened or inactive microbes, or parts of them, into the body. What is the main purpose of vaccination? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"टीका शरीर में दुर्बल या निष्क्रिय सूक्ष्मजीवों अथवा उनके भागों को पहुँचा सकता है। टीकाकरण का मुख्य उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increase blood pressure","hi":"रक्तचाप बढ़ाना"},"2":{"en":"Develop immunity against a specific disease","hi":"किसी विशिष्ट रोग के विरुद्ध प्रतिरक्षा विकसित करना"},"3":{"en":"Destroy red blood cells","hi":"लाल रक्त कोशिकाओं को नष्ट करना"},"4":{"en":"Temporarily stop digestion","hi":"पाचन अस्थायी रूप से रोकना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Develop immunity against a specific disease</b><br>A vaccine introduces weakened, killed or fragmentary antigens of a pathogen so that the body produces <b>antibodies and memory cells</b>, thereby developing <b>immunity against that specific disease</b> without causing the disease itself.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The principle of vaccination was demonstrated by <b>Edward Jenner</b> (smallpox, 1796) and developed by <b>Louis Pasteur</b>, who coined the term vaccine from <i>vacca</i> (cow).<br>• Types of vaccines are <b>live attenuated, inactivated, toxoid, subunit and mRNA vaccines</b>; BCG, OPV and MMR are live attenuated, while DPT contains toxoids.<br>• In India, the <b>Universal Immunisation Programme</b> (1985) and Mission Indradhanush cover vaccines against BCG, polio, measles, hepatitis B, DPT, tetanus and rotavirus.<br>• Vaccines produce <b>active acquired immunity</b>, whereas injectable antibodies give passive immunity; herd immunity protects the unvaccinated part of a population.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – किसी विशिष्ट रोग के विरुद्ध प्रतिरक्षा विकसित करना</b><br>टीका रोगजनक के दुर्बल, मृत या खंडित प्रतिजनों को शरीर में पहुँचाता है, जिससे शरीर <b>प्रतिरक्षी व स्मृति कोशिकाएँ</b> बनाता है और रोग उत्पन्न हुए बिना <b>उस विशिष्ट रोग के विरुद्ध प्रतिरक्षा</b> विकसित हो जाती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• टीकाकरण का सिद्धांत <b>एडवर्ड जेनर</b> (चेचक, 1796) ने प्रदर्शित किया तथा <b>लुई पाश्चर</b> ने विकसित किया, जिन्होंने <i>वैक्सा</i> (गाय) से \"वैक्सीन\" शब्द बनाया।<br>• टीकों के प्रकार हैं — <b>जीवित दुर्बल, निष्क्रिय, विषमुक्त, उप-इकाई तथा mRNA टीके</b>; BCG, OPV व MMR जीवित दुर्बल हैं, जबकि DPT में विषमुक्त (टॉक्सॉइड) होते हैं।<br>• भारत में <b>सार्वभौमिक टीकाकरण कार्यक्रम</b> (1985) तथा मिशन इंद्रधनुष BCG, पोलियो, खसरा, हेपेटाइटिस B, DPT, टिटनेस व रोटावायरस के टीके देते हैं।<br>• टीके <b>सक्रिय अर्जित प्रतिरक्षा</b> बनाते हैं, जबकि इंजेक्शन वाले प्रतिरक्षी निष्क्रिय प्रतिरक्षा देते हैं; समूह प्रतिरक्षा (herd immunity) बिना टीके वाले भाग की रक्षा करती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000075031","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The base of a right prism is a rhombus with diagonals 8 cm and 10 cm. The height of the prism is 12 cm. Find the volume. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक लंब प्रिज्म का आधार एक समचतुर्भुज है जिसके विकर्ण 8 cm और 10 cm हैं। प्रिज्म की ऊँचाई 12 cm है। आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"384 cm³"},"2":{"en":"420 cm³"},"3":{"en":"480 cm³"},"4":{"en":"540 cm³"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"150\" height=\"110\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 110\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 55L75 15L130 55L75 95Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 55H130M75 15V95\"/><path d=\"M75 48h7v7\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"53\" y=\"51\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"77\">8</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">h = 12</text></g></svg><br>Base area = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times d_1 \\times d_2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 8 \\times 10 = 40\\) cm²<br>Volume = Base area × Height = \\(40 \\times 12 = \\boxed{480}\\) cm³<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 480 cm³.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"150\" height=\"110\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 110\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 55L75 15L130 55L75 95Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 55H130M75 15V95\"/><path d=\"M75 48h7v7\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"53\" y=\"51\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"77\">8</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">h = 12</text></g></svg><br>आधार का क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times d_1 \\times d_2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 8 \\times 10 = 40\\) cm²<br>आयतन = आधार का क्षेत्रफल × ऊँचाई = \\(40 \\times 12 = \\boxed{480}\\) cm³<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 480 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000075032","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a triangle, the centroid divides each median in the ratio 2:1. What is the distance between the centroid and the incenter in an equilateral triangle? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक त्रिभुज में, केन्द्रक प्रत्येक माध्यिका को 2:1 के अनुपात में विभाजित करता है। एक समबाहु त्रिभुज में केन्द्रक और अंतःकेंद्र के बीच की दूरी क्या है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Equal to the altitude","hi":"शीर्षलंब के बराबर"},"2":{"en":"Half the altitude","hi":"शीर्षलंब का आधा"},"3":{"en":"Zero","hi":"शून्य"},"4":{"en":"One-third of the altitude","hi":"शीर्षलंब का एक-तिहाई"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"205\" height=\"174\" viewBox=\"0 0 205 174\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M100 20L25 150H175Z\"/><path d=\"M25 150L100 107L175 150\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"154\">B</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"154\">C</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"101\" text-anchor=\"middle\">G = I</text></g></svg><br>In an equilateral triangle each median is also an angle bisector and an altitude.<br>So the centroid (G) and the incenter (I) are the same point.<br>Distance GI = \\(\\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Zero.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"205\" height=\"174\" viewBox=\"0 0 205 174\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M100 20L25 150H175Z\"/><path d=\"M25 150L100 107L175 150\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"154\">B</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"154\">C</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"101\" text-anchor=\"middle\">G = I</text></g></svg><br>समबाहु त्रिभुज में प्रत्येक माध्यिका कोण समद्विभाजक और शीर्षलंब भी होती है।<br>अतः केन्द्रक (G) और अंतःकेंद्र (I) एक ही बिंदु हैं।<br>दूरी GI = \\(\\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): शून्य है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000075033","section":"MATH","topic":"LCM and HCF","question":{"en":"What is the smallest number that is a perfect square and is also divisible by 6, 15, and 20? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह सबसे छोटी संख्या कौन-सी है जो एक पूर्ण वर्ग है और 6, 15 तथा 20 से भी विभाज्य है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"700"},"2":{"en":"900"},"3":{"en":"600"},"4":{"en":"800"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"LCM(6, 15, 20) = 60 = \\(2^2 \\times 3 \\times 5\\)<br>To make it a perfect square, multiply by 3 × 5 = 15<br>\\(60 \\times 15 = \\boxed{900}\\) \\(= 30^2\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 900.</b>","hi":"LCM(6, 15, 20) = 60 = \\(2^2 \\times 3 \\times 5\\)<br>पूर्ण वर्ग बनाने के लिए 3 × 5 = 15 से गुणा करें<br>\\(60 \\times 15 = \\boxed{900}\\) \\(= 30^2\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 900 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000075034","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"A and B started a business by investing capital in the ratio 5 : 3. At the end of 6 months, C joined them with an investment equal to the average of A and B. If the profit at the end of the year is ₹18,000, find C's share. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A और B ने 5 : 3 के अनुपात में पूँजी लगाकर एक व्यवसाय शुरू किया। 6 महीने के अंत में, C, A और B की पूँजी के औसत के बराबर निवेश के साथ उनसे जुड़ गया। यदि वर्ष के अंत में लाभ ₹18,000 है, तो C का हिस्सा ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹3,600"},"2":{"en":"₹4,200"},"3":{"en":"₹5,000"},"4":{"en":"₹6,100"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A = 5, B = 3, C = \\(\\frac{5 + 3}{2} = 4\\)<br>A : B : C = \\(5 \\times 12 : 3 \\times 12 : 4 \\times 6 = 60 : 36 : 24 = 5 : 3 : 2\\)<br>C's share = \\(\\frac{2}{10} \\times 18000 = \\boxed{3600}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹3,600.</b>","hi":"A = 5, B = 3, C = \\(\\frac{5 + 3}{2} = 4\\)<br>A : B : C = \\(5 \\times 12 : 3 \\times 12 : 4 \\times 6 = 60 : 36 : 24 = 5 : 3 : 2\\)<br>C का हिस्सा = \\(\\frac{2}{10} \\times 18000 = \\boxed{3600}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹3,600 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000075035","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"An amount of ₹5,000 is invested at 12% compound interest. What will be the amount after 2 years? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"₹5,000 की राशि 12% चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर निवेश की जाती है। 2 वर्ष बाद मिश्रधन कितना होगा? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹5972"},"2":{"en":"₹6172"},"3":{"en":"₹6072"},"4":{"en":"₹6272"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Amount = \\(5000 \\times \\left(1 + \\frac{12}{100}\\right)^2 = 5000 \\times 1.2544\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{6272}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹6272.</b>","hi":"मिश्रधन = \\(5000 \\times \\left(1 + \\frac{12}{100}\\right)^2 = 5000 \\times 1.2544\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{6272}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹6272 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000075036","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A large room has an area of \\(24\\sqrt{3}\\) m². It is to be covered with regular hexagonal tiles of side 20 cm. How many full tiles are required to cover the area (ignoring gaps)? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक बड़े कमरे का क्षेत्रफल \\(24\\sqrt{3}\\) m² है। इसे 20 cm भुजा वाली सम षट्भुजाकार टाइलों से ढकना है। क्षेत्रफल को ढकने के लिए कितनी पूरी टाइलों की आवश्यकता होगी (रिक्त स्थानों को अनदेखा करें)? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"400 tiles","hi":"400 टाइलें"},"2":{"en":"435 tiles","hi":"435 टाइलें"},"3":{"en":"390 tiles","hi":"390 टाइलें"},"4":{"en":"455 tiles","hi":"455 टाइलें"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"150\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"72\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M130 72L102 24L48 24L20 72L47 120L102 120Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M75 72H130M75 72L102 24\"/><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"72\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"102\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"42\">20</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"86\">O</text></g></svg><br>Area of one tile = \\(\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 20^2 = 600\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²<br>Room = \\(24\\sqrt{3} \\times 10000 = 240000\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²<br>Tiles = \\(\\frac{240000\\sqrt{3}}{600\\sqrt{3}} = \\boxed{400}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 400 tiles.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"150\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"72\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M130 72L102 24L48 24L20 72L47 120L102 120Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M75 72H130M75 72L102 24\"/><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"72\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"102\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"42\">20</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"86\">O</text></g></svg><br>एक टाइल का क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 20^2 = 600\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²<br>कमरा = \\(24\\sqrt{3} \\times 10000 = 240000\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²<br>टाइलें = \\(\\frac{240000\\sqrt{3}}{600\\sqrt{3}} = \\boxed{400}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 400 टाइलें है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000075037","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A cone-shaped tank has a radius of 5 cm and a slant height of 14 cm. If the cost of painting is ₹18 per cm², find the approximate cost to paint the tank. (\\(\\pi = 3.14\\)) [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक शंकु के आकार की टंकी की त्रिज्या 5 cm और तिर्यक ऊँचाई 14 cm है। यदि पेंट करने की लागत ₹18 प्रति cm² है, तो टंकी को पेंट करने की लगभग लागत ज्ञात कीजिए। (\\(\\pi = 3.14\\)) [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹6,000"},"2":{"en":"₹6,369"},"3":{"en":"₹5,369"},"4":{"en":"₹5,400"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">h</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\">14</text></g></svg><br>The closed tank is painted on its whole surface (curved surface + base)<br>TSA = \\(\\pi r(l + r) = 3.14 \\times 5 \\times 19 = 298.3\\) cm²<br>Cost = \\(298.3 \\times 18 = 5369.4 \\approx \\boxed{5369}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹5,369.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">h</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\">14</text></g></svg><br>बंद टंकी की पूरी सतह (वक्र पृष्ठ + आधार) पेंट की जाती है<br>संपूर्ण पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\pi r(l + r) = 3.14 \\times 5 \\times 19 = 298.3\\) cm²<br>लागत = \\(298.3 \\times 18 = 5369.4 \\approx \\boxed{5369}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹5,369 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000075038","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"If the area of a quadrant of a circle is 16π cm², find the radius of the circle. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि एक वृत्त के चतुर्थांश का क्षेत्रफल 16π cm² है, तो वृत्त की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4 cm"},"2":{"en":"3 cm"},"3":{"en":"7 cm"},"4":{"en":"8 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"130\" height=\"132\" viewBox=\"0 0 130 132\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 20L20 110H110A90 90 0 0 0 20 20\"/><path d=\"M38 110A18 18 0 0 0 20 92\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"65\" y=\"125\" text-anchor=\"middle\">r</text><text x=\"41\" y=\"105\">90°</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"114\">O</text></g></svg><br>Area of quadrant = \\(\\frac{\\pi r^2}{4} = 16\\pi\\)<br>\\(r^2 = 64\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{8}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"130\" height=\"132\" viewBox=\"0 0 130 132\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 20L20 110H110A90 90 0 0 0 20 20\"/><path d=\"M38 110A18 18 0 0 0 20 92\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"65\" y=\"125\" text-anchor=\"middle\">r</text><text x=\"41\" y=\"105\">90°</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"114\">O</text></g></svg><br>चतुर्थांश का क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{\\pi r^2}{4} = 16\\pi\\)<br>\\(r^2 = 64\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{8}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000075039","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"An article is sold at 20% profit. If its cost price and selling price are both reduced by ₹100, the profit would be 4% more. Find the original cost price. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वस्तु 20% लाभ पर बेची जाती है। यदि इसके क्रय मूल्य और विक्रय मूल्य दोनों में ₹100 की कमी कर दी जाए, तो लाभ 4% अधिक होगा। मूल क्रय मूल्य ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹200"},"2":{"en":"₹400"},"3":{"en":"₹800"},"4":{"en":"₹600"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let CP = x → profit = 0.2x (profit stays same when both are reduced by 100)<br>New profit % = 24% → \\(\\frac{0.2x}{x - 100} = \\frac{24}{100}\\)<br>\\(20x = 24x - 2400 \\Rightarrow 4x = 2400\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{600}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹600.</b>","hi":"माना क्रय मूल्य = x → लाभ = 0.2x (दोनों में 100 घटाने पर लाभ वही रहता है)<br>नया लाभ % = 24% → \\(\\frac{0.2x}{x - 100} = \\frac{24}{100}\\)<br>\\(20x = 24x - 2400 \\Rightarrow 4x = 2400\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{600}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹600 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000075040","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"By selling 45 apples for ₹160, a vendor loses 20%. How many apples should he sell for ₹112 to gain 20% in the entire transaction? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"45 सेब ₹160 में बेचने पर एक विक्रेता को 20% हानि होती है। पूरे सौदे में 20% लाभ पाने के लिए उसे ₹112 में कितने सेब बेचने चाहिए? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"24"},"2":{"en":"21"},"3":{"en":"26"},"4":{"en":"28"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"CP of 45 apples = \\(\\frac{160}{80} \\times 100 = 200\\)<br>For 20% gain, CP of apples sold for 112 = \\(\\frac{112}{120} \\times 100 = \\frac{280}{3}\\)<br>Apples = \\(\\frac{280}{3} \\times \\frac{45}{200} = \\boxed{21}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 21.</b>","hi":"45 सेबों का क्रय मूल्य = \\(\\frac{160}{80} \\times 100 = 200\\)<br>20% लाभ के लिए, 112 में बेचे गए सेबों का क्रय मूल्य = \\(\\frac{112}{120} \\times 100 = \\frac{280}{3}\\)<br>सेब = \\(\\frac{280}{3} \\times \\frac{45}{200} = \\boxed{21}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 21 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000075041","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A man standing on a tower sees a train approaching. The angle of depression changes from 30° to 60° in 14 minutes. Find the time taken by the train to reach the base of the tower. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक मीनार पर खड़ा व्यक्ति एक ट्रेन को आते हुए देखता है। अवनमन कोण 14 मिनट में 30° से 60° हो जाता है। ट्रेन को मीनार के आधार तक पहुँचने में लगने वाला समय ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6 minutes","hi":"6 मिनट"},"2":{"en":"10 minutes","hi":"10 मिनट"},"3":{"en":"9 minutes","hi":"9 मिनट"},"4":{"en":"7 minutes","hi":"7 मिनट"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"262\" height=\"159\" viewBox=\"0 0 262 159\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M50 20V124H230ZM50 20L110 124\"/><path d=\"M50 116h8v8\"/><path d=\"M94 124A16 16 0 0 1 102 110\"/><path d=\"M214 124A16 16 0 0 1 216 116\"/><path d=\"M110 143H230\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"45\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"end\">B</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">D</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\">h</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"118\">60°</text><text x=\"233\" y=\"118\">30°</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"153\" text-anchor=\"middle\">14 min</text></g></svg><br>Angles of elevation from C and D equal the angles of depression.<br>BC = \\(h\\sqrt{3}\\), BD = \\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\) → CD = \\(\\frac{3h - h}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{2h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>CD : BD = 2 : 1 → CD takes 14 min, so BD takes \\(\\frac{14}{2} = \\boxed{7}\\) minutes<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 7 minutes.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"262\" height=\"159\" viewBox=\"0 0 262 159\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M50 20V124H230ZM50 20L110 124\"/><path d=\"M50 116h8v8\"/><path d=\"M94 124A16 16 0 0 1 102 110\"/><path d=\"M214 124A16 16 0 0 1 216 116\"/><path d=\"M110 143H230\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"45\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"end\">B</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">D</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\">h</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"118\">60°</text><text x=\"233\" y=\"118\">30°</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"153\" text-anchor=\"middle\">14 min</text></g></svg><br>C और D से उन्नयन कोण, अवनमन कोणों के बराबर हैं।<br>BC = \\(h\\sqrt{3}\\), BD = \\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\) → CD = \\(\\frac{3h - h}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{2h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>CD : BD = 2 : 1 → CD में 14 मिनट, अतः BD में \\(\\frac{14}{2} = \\boxed{7}\\) मिनट<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 7 मिनट है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000075042","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Angles x and y are supplementary. y is 40° more than one-fourth of its supplementary angle. Find the value of the complement of half of x. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कोण x और y संपूरक हैं। y अपने संपूरक कोण के एक-चौथाई से 40° अधिक है। x के आधे का पूरक कोण ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"22°"},"2":{"en":"90°"},"3":{"en":"34°"},"4":{"en":"45°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(x + y = 180^\\circ\\) and \\(y = \\frac{x}{4} + 40^\\circ\\)<br>\\(x + \\frac{x}{4} + 40^\\circ = 180^\\circ \\Rightarrow \\frac{5x}{4} = 140^\\circ \\Rightarrow x = 112^\\circ\\)<br>Half of x = 56° → Complement = \\(90^\\circ - 56^\\circ = \\boxed{34^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 34°.</b>","hi":"\\(x + y = 180^\\circ\\) और \\(y = \\frac{x}{4} + 40^\\circ\\)<br>\\(x + \\frac{x}{4} + 40^\\circ = 180^\\circ \\Rightarrow \\frac{5x}{4} = 140^\\circ \\Rightarrow x = 112^\\circ\\)<br>x का आधा = 56° → पूरक कोण = \\(90^\\circ - 56^\\circ = \\boxed{34^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 34° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000075043","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(0^\\circ \\lt \\theta \\lt 90^\\circ\\), find the value of \\(1 + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\tan\\theta + \\sin\\theta}{\\tan\\theta - \\sin\\theta}}\\). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(0^\\circ \\lt \\theta \\lt 90^\\circ\\) है, तो \\(1 + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\tan\\theta + \\sin\\theta}{\\tan\\theta - \\sin\\theta}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(1 + \\cosec\\theta + \\cot\\theta\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(1 + \\cosec\\theta - \\cot\\theta\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(1 + \\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(1 + \\sec\\theta - \\tan\\theta\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\tan\\theta + \\sin\\theta}{\\tan\\theta - \\sin\\theta} = \\frac{1 + \\cos\\theta}{1 - \\cos\\theta} = \\frac{(1 + \\cos\\theta)^2}{\\sin^2\\theta}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{\\ \\ } = \\frac{1 + \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} = \\cosec\\theta + \\cot\\theta\\)<br>Value = \\(\\boxed{1 + \\cosec\\theta + \\cot\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(1 + \\cosec\\theta + \\cot\\theta\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\tan\\theta + \\sin\\theta}{\\tan\\theta - \\sin\\theta} = \\frac{1 + \\cos\\theta}{1 - \\cos\\theta} = \\frac{(1 + \\cos\\theta)^2}{\\sin^2\\theta}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{\\ \\ } = \\frac{1 + \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} = \\cosec\\theta + \\cot\\theta\\)<br>मान = \\(\\boxed{1 + \\cosec\\theta + \\cot\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(1 + \\cosec\\theta + \\cot\\theta\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000075044","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"If a solid sphere of radius 9 cm is melted and recast into a cylinder with a base radius of 3 cm, what will be the height of the cylinder? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 9 cm त्रिज्या वाले एक ठोस गोले को पिघलाकर 3 cm आधार त्रिज्या वाले एक बेलन में ढाला जाए, तो बेलन की ऊँचाई क्या होगी? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"102 cm"},"2":{"en":"108 cm"},"3":{"en":"254 cm"},"4":{"en":"274 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"135\" height=\"125\" viewBox=\"0 0 135 125\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M65 65H115\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"61\">9</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">3</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">h</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi (9)^3 = \\pi (3)^2 h\\)<br>\\(972 = 9h\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{108}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 108 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"135\" height=\"125\" viewBox=\"0 0 135 125\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M65 65H115\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"61\">9</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">3</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">h</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi (9)^3 = \\pi (3)^2 h\\)<br>\\(972 = 9h\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{108}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 108 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000075045","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, points D and E lie on AB and AC such that DE is parallel to BC. If \\(\\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{1}{2}\\) and AE = 6 cm, find AC. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, बिंदु D और E क्रमशः AB और AC पर इस प्रकार स्थित हैं कि DE, BC के समांतर है। यदि \\(\\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{1}{2}\\) और AE = 6 cm है, तो AC ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"14 cm"},"2":{"en":"18 cm"},"3":{"en":"20 cm"},"4":{"en":"22 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M120 18L40 150H210ZM93 62L150 62\"/><path d=\"M119 58l5 4-5 4M122 146l5 4-5 4\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"154\">B</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"154\">C</text><text x=\"81\" y=\"66\">D</text><text x=\"155\" y=\"66\">E</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"44\" text-anchor=\"end\">1</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\">2</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"44\">6</text><text x=\"187\" y=\"110\">EC</text></g></svg><br>DE ∥ BC → \\(\\frac{AE}{EC} = \\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>EC = \\(2 \\times 6 = 12\\) cm<br>AC = 6 + 12 = \\(\\boxed{18}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 18 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M120 18L40 150H210ZM93 62L150 62\"/><path d=\"M119 58l5 4-5 4M122 146l5 4-5 4\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"154\">B</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"154\">C</text><text x=\"81\" y=\"66\">D</text><text x=\"155\" y=\"66\">E</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"44\" text-anchor=\"end\">1</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\">2</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"44\">6</text><text x=\"187\" y=\"110\">EC</text></g></svg><br>DE ∥ BC → \\(\\frac{AE}{EC} = \\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>EC = \\(2 \\times 6 = 12\\) cm<br>AC = 6 + 12 = \\(\\boxed{18}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 18 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000075046","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"The square root of 1.44×0.81 is: [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1.44×0.81 का वर्गमूल है: [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.98"},"2":{"en":"1.08"},"3":{"en":"1.18"},"4":{"en":"1.28"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{1.44 \\times 0.81} = \\sqrt{1.44} \\times \\sqrt{0.81}\\)<br>\\(= 1.2 \\times 0.9 = \\boxed{1.08}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.08.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{1.44 \\times 0.81} = \\sqrt{1.44} \\times \\sqrt{0.81}\\)<br>\\(= 1.2 \\times 0.9 = \\boxed{1.08}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1.08 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000075047","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A medium-sized furniture manufacturer borrowed a certain amount from a nationalized bank to expand its production unit. The loan was sanctioned at a fixed rate of simple interest. After 8 years, the total amount repaid was ₹7,20,000, which included ₹2,40,000 as interest. Had the company borrowed ₹1,50,000 more at the same rate and for the same duration, determine the total repayment amount. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक मध्यम आकार के फर्नीचर निर्माता ने अपनी उत्पादन इकाई के विस्तार के लिए एक राष्ट्रीयकृत बैंक से एक निश्चित राशि उधार ली। ऋण साधारण ब्याज की एक निश्चित दर पर स्वीकृत किया गया। 8 वर्ष बाद, कुल चुकाई गई राशि ₹7,20,000 थी, जिसमें ₹2,40,000 ब्याज शामिल था। यदि कंपनी ने समान दर और समान अवधि के लिए ₹1,50,000 अधिक उधार लिए होते, तो कुल चुकाई जाने वाली राशि ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹8,66,000"},"2":{"en":"₹9,45,000"},"3":{"en":"₹7,22,000"},"4":{"en":"₹6,66,000"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Principal = 7,20,000 − 2,40,000 = ₹4,80,000<br>Amount/Principal = \\(\\frac{720000}{480000} = 1.5\\) (same rate, same time)<br>New principal = ₹6,30,000<br>New amount = \\(630000 \\times 1.5 = \\boxed{945000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹9,45,000.</b>","hi":"मूलधन = 7,20,000 − 2,40,000 = ₹4,80,000<br>मिश्रधन/मूलधन = \\(\\frac{720000}{480000} = 1.5\\) (समान दर, समान समय)<br>नया मूलधन = ₹6,30,000<br>नया मिश्रधन = \\(630000 \\times 1.5 = \\boxed{945000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹9,45,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000075048","section":"MATH","topic":"Pipe and Cistern","question":{"en":"Pipe X can fill a tank in 16 minutes and pipe Y can fill it in in 24 minutes. A drainpipe Z can empty it in x minutes. All the three pipes are opened simultaneously at a particular point of time and after 8 minutes, pipe Z is closed. The tank becomes exactly full 4 minutes later. Find the time taken by pipe Z to empty the entirely filled tank alone. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पाइप X एक टंकी को 16 मिनट में और पाइप Y उसे 24 मिनट में भर सकता है। एक निकास पाइप Z उसे x मिनट में खाली कर सकता है। तीनों पाइप एक निश्चित समय पर एक साथ खोले जाते हैं और 8 मिनट बाद पाइप Z बंद कर दिया जाता है। इसके 4 मिनट बाद टंकी ठीक पूरी भर जाती है। पूरी भरी टंकी को अकेले खाली करने में पाइप Z द्वारा लिया गया समय ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25 minutes","hi":"25 मिनट"},"2":{"en":"28 minutes","hi":"28 मिनट"},"3":{"en":"30 minutes","hi":"30 मिनट"},"4":{"en":"32 minutes","hi":"32 मिनट"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Tank = LCM(16, 24) = 48 units → X = 3/min, Y = 2/min<br>X and Y run 12 minutes: \\(5 \\times 12 = 60\\) units<br>Z removed 60 − 48 = 12 units in 8 minutes → 1.5/min<br>Z alone = \\(\\frac{48}{1.5} = \\boxed{32}\\) minutes<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 32 minutes.</b>","hi":"टंकी = LCM(16, 24) = 48 इकाई → X = 3/मिनट, Y = 2/मिनट<br>X और Y 12 मिनट चले: \\(5 \\times 12 = 60\\) इकाई<br>Z ने 8 मिनट में 60 − 48 = 12 इकाई निकालीं → 1.5/मिनट<br>Z अकेले = \\(\\frac{48}{1.5} = \\boxed{32}\\) मिनट<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 32 मिनट है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000075049","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"Two drones, Alpha and Beta, are tasked with mapping a large valley. Alpha can map the entire valley alone in 10 hrs of flight, while Beta alone can do that in 15 hours of flight. Alpha's battery lasts for exactly 2 hours of continuous flight, after which it requires 1 hour of recharge. Beta's battery lasts for 3 hours of continuous flight, after which it requires 2 hours of recharge. Both start the mapping at the same time in fully charged condition. How much time will it take to completely map the valley? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो ड्रोन, अल्फा और बीटा, एक बड़ी घाटी का मानचित्रण करने का कार्य करते हैं। अल्फा अकेले 10 घंटे की उड़ान में पूरी घाटी का मानचित्रण कर सकता है, जबकि बीटा अकेले यह 15 घंटे की उड़ान में कर सकता है। अल्फा की बैटरी लगातार ठीक 2 घंटे की उड़ान तक चलती है, जिसके बाद उसे 1 घंटे रिचार्ज की आवश्यकता होती है। बीटा की बैटरी लगातार 3 घंटे की उड़ान तक चलती है, जिसके बाद उसे 2 घंटे रिचार्ज की आवश्यकता होती है। दोनों पूरी तरह चार्ज स्थिति में एक साथ मानचित्रण शुरू करते हैं। घाटी का पूरा मानचित्रण करने में कितना समय लगेगा? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6 hrs","hi":"6 घंटे"},"2":{"en":"9 hrs","hi":"9 घंटे"},"3":{"en":"7 hrs","hi":"7 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"8 hrs","hi":"8 घंटे"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Work = LCM(10, 15) = 30 units → Alpha = 3/hr, Beta = 2/hr<br>Alpha flies hours 1–2, 4–5, 7–8; Beta flies hours 1–3, 6–8<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Hour</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Work</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Total</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td></tr></table>30 units done at the end of hour 8 → \\(\\boxed{8}\\) hrs<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8 hrs.</b>","hi":"कार्य = LCM(10, 15) = 30 इकाई → अल्फा = 3/घंटा, बीटा = 2/घंटा<br>अल्फा घंटे 1–2, 4–5, 7–8 में उड़ता है; बीटा घंटे 1–3, 6–8 में<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">घंटा</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">कार्य</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">कुल</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td></tr></table>8वें घंटे के अंत में 30 इकाई पूरी → \\(\\boxed{8}\\) घंटे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8 घंटे है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000075050","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\cos^2\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\) and \\(0^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 90^\\circ\\), how many distinct values of \\(\\theta\\) satisfy this equation? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\cos^2\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\) और \\(0^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 90^\\circ\\) है, तो \\(\\theta\\) के कितने भिन्न मान इस समीकरण को संतुष्ट करते हैं? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"6"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos\\theta = \\pm\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\); in 0° to 90°, cos θ ≥ 0 → \\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br>\\(\\theta = 45^\\circ\\) only<br>Number of values = \\(\\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos\\theta = \\pm\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\); 0° से 90° में cos θ ≥ 0 → \\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br>केवल \\(\\theta = 45^\\circ\\)<br>मानों की संख्या = \\(\\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000075051","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Evaluate: \\(\\tan 42^\\circ \\tan 48^\\circ - \\cot 48^\\circ \\cot 42^\\circ\\) [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: \\(\\tan 42^\\circ \\tan 48^\\circ - \\cot 48^\\circ \\cot 42^\\circ\\) [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"0"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"−1"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan 48^\\circ = \\cot 42^\\circ\\) → \\(\\tan 42^\\circ \\tan 48^\\circ = 1\\)<br>\\(\\cot 48^\\circ = \\tan 42^\\circ\\) → \\(\\cot 48^\\circ \\cot 42^\\circ = 1\\)<br>Value = 1 − 1 = \\(\\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 0.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan 48^\\circ = \\cot 42^\\circ\\) → \\(\\tan 42^\\circ \\tan 48^\\circ = 1\\)<br>\\(\\cot 48^\\circ = \\tan 42^\\circ\\) → \\(\\cot 48^\\circ \\cot 42^\\circ = 1\\)<br>मान = 1 − 1 = \\(\\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000075052","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(a + b + c = 17\\) and \\(ab + bc + ca = 21\\), what is the value of \\(a^3 + b^3 + c^3 - 3abc\\)? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(a + b + c = 17\\) और \\(ab + bc + ca = 21\\) है, तो \\(a^3 + b^3 + c^3 - 3abc\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3100"},"2":{"en":"3842"},"3":{"en":"4022"},"4":{"en":"5032"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(a^3 + b^3 + c^3 - 3abc = (a + b + c)[(a + b + c)^2 - 3(ab + bc + ca)]\\)<br>\\(= 17 \\times (289 - 63) = 17 \\times 226\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3842}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3842.</b>","hi":"\\(a^3 + b^3 + c^3 - 3abc = (a + b + c)[(a + b + c)^2 - 3(ab + bc + ca)]\\)<br>\\(= 17 \\times (289 - 63) = 17 \\times 226\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3842}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3842 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000075053","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(a + b = 17\\) and \\(ab = 60\\), then find the value of \\((a - b)^4\\). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(a + b = 17\\) और \\(ab = 60\\) है, तो \\((a - b)^4\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"83521"},"2":{"en":"28561"},"3":{"en":"49"},"4":{"en":"2401"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\((a - b)^2 = (a + b)^2 - 4ab = 289 - 240 = 49\\)<br>\\((a - b)^4 = 49^2 = \\boxed{2401}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2401.</b>","hi":"\\((a - b)^2 = (a + b)^2 - 4ab = 289 - 240 = 49\\)<br>\\((a - b)^4 = 49^2 = \\boxed{2401}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 2401 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000075054","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A regular hexagonal prism has a base side length of 5 m and a height of 10 m. A regular hexagonal pyramid with a height of 4 m shares the top base of the prism. Find the total volume of the resulting composite solid. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक सम षट्भुजाकार प्रिज्म के आधार की भुजा 5 m और ऊँचाई 10 m है। 4 m ऊँचाई वाला एक सम षट्भुजाकार पिरामिड प्रिज्म के ऊपरी आधार पर बना है। परिणामी संयुक्त ठोस का कुल आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(425\\sqrt{3}\\) m³"},"2":{"en":"\\(424\\sqrt{2}\\) m³"},"3":{"en":"\\(354\\sqrt{2}\\) m³"},"4":{"en":"\\(368\\sqrt{3}\\) m³"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Base area = \\(\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 5^2 = \\frac{75\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\) m²<br>Prism = \\(\\frac{75\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 10 = 375\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>Pyramid = \\(\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{75\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 4 = 50\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>Total = \\(\\boxed{425\\sqrt{3}}\\) m³<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(425\\sqrt{3}\\) m³.</b>","hi":"आधार का क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 5^2 = \\frac{75\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\) m²<br>प्रिज्म = \\(\\frac{75\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 10 = 375\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>पिरामिड = \\(\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{75\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 4 = 50\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>कुल = \\(\\boxed{425\\sqrt{3}}\\) m³<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(425\\sqrt{3}\\) m³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000075055","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(a = \\sqrt{5 + 2\\sqrt{6}}\\) and \\(b = \\sqrt{5 - 2\\sqrt{6}}\\), evaluate the value of the following expression:<br>\\(a^6 + b^6\\). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(a = \\sqrt{5 + 2\\sqrt{6}}\\) और \\(b = \\sqrt{5 - 2\\sqrt{6}}\\) है, तो निम्नलिखित व्यंजक का मान ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>\\(a^6 + b^6\\)। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"970"},"2":{"en":"1000"},"3":{"en":"1030"},"4":{"en":"940"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(a^2 = 5 + 2\\sqrt{6},\\ b^2 = 5 - 2\\sqrt{6}\\) → \\(a^2 + b^2 = 10,\\ a^2b^2 = 25 - 24 = 1\\)<br>\\(a^6 + b^6 = (a^2 + b^2)^3 - 3a^2b^2(a^2 + b^2)\\)<br>\\(= 1000 - 3 \\times 1 \\times 10 = \\boxed{970}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 970.</b>","hi":"\\(a^2 = 5 + 2\\sqrt{6},\\ b^2 = 5 - 2\\sqrt{6}\\) → \\(a^2 + b^2 = 10,\\ a^2b^2 = 25 - 24 = 1\\)<br>\\(a^6 + b^6 = (a^2 + b^2)^3 - 3a^2b^2(a^2 + b^2)\\)<br>\\(= 1000 - 3 \\times 1 \\times 10 = \\boxed{970}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 970 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000075056","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the correct transformation of the sentence into direct speech.<br>She wondered if she should apply for the scholarship. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She asked, “Do I apply for the scholarship?”"},"2":{"en":"She said, “Should I apply for the scholarship?”"},"3":{"en":"She wondered, “Will I apply for the scholarship?”"},"4":{"en":"She said, “I should apply for the scholarship.”"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Wondered if” represents an internal yes/no question.</b><br>The direct thought is “Should I apply for the scholarship?”<br>A changes the modal and meaning; C changes to “will.”<br>D turns the question into a statement.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): She said, “Should I apply for the scholarship?”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000075057","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>The Nobel Prize in Literature<br>P. for its powerful storytelling and deep philosophical insights<br>Q. was awarded to the renowned author<br>R. whose latest novel explores human resilience<br>S. in the face of adversity and historical struggles [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PRSQ"},"2":{"en":"QRSP"},"3":{"en":"PRQS"},"4":{"en":"QSPR"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRSP</b><br>Q supplies the passive predicate “was awarded to the renowned author.”<br>R introduces the author’s latest novel, and S completes what it explores.<br>P gives the qualities for which the novel or authorship is recognized.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): QRSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000075058","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"People who do not lay out their money carefully, soon come to grief. What does “come to grief” mean? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To experience failure or trouble"},"2":{"en":"To become very rich"},"3":{"en":"To achieve great success"},"4":{"en":"To find unexpected luck"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Come to grief (विपत्ति में पड़ना) = suffer failure, loss or trouble.</b><br>Careless handling of money can lead to financial trouble.<br>Example: “His reckless investment came to grief.”<br>Wealth, success and unexpected luck are positive outcomes and do not fit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): To experience failure or trouble.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000075059","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Complete the sentence by choosing a suitable word to fill in the blank.<br>That she, of all people, ___ the one to criticize others is baffling. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"are"},"2":{"en":"be"},"3":{"en":"were"},"4":{"en":"is"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The pronoun “she” takes the singular present verb “is.”</b><br>The parenthetical “of all people” does not affect agreement.<br>Completed sentence: “That she, of all people, <b>is</b> the one to criticize others is baffling.”<br>“Are” and “were” do not fit; “be” is not the finite indicative form.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): is.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000075060","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the word in this sentence that contains an error.<br>He was accused for cheating in the final exam. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"cheating"},"2":{"en":"for"},"3":{"en":"accused"},"4":{"en":"final"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Accuse somebody of something” is the fixed construction.</b><br>The erroneous word is “for,” which must become “of.”<br>Correct sentence: “He was accused <b>of</b> cheating in the final exam.”<br>The remaining words are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): for.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000075061","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. Many birds migrate seasonally, traveling thousands of kilometers to find suitable breeding or feeding grounds.<br>2. Scientists have discovered that birds use a combination of celestial navigation, Earth's magnetic field, and learned landmarks to guide their journeys.<br>3. This behavior is often triggered by changes in daylight duration and temperature, signaling the need to relocate.<br>4. Some species, such as the Arctic Tern, undertake the longest migration, covering distances between the Arctic and Antarctic.<br>5. Understanding bird migration patterns is crucial for conservation efforts, as climate change and habitat destruction pose growing threats. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-1-4-3-5"},"2":{"en":"1-3-2-4-5"},"3":{"en":"3-4-2-5-1"},"4":{"en":"3-2-1-5-4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-3-2-4-5</b><br>Sentence 1 introduces seasonal migration, and sentence 3 explains what triggers “this behavior.”<br>Sentence 2 describes navigation methods; sentence 4 gives the Arctic Tern example.<br>Sentence 5 concludes with the conservation importance of migration research.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1-3-2-4-5.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000075062","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence by selecting the appropriate preposition from the following options.<br>We need to plan carefully to stay ___ of our competition. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"for"},"2":{"en":"in"},"3":{"en":"beyond"},"4":{"en":"ahead"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Ahead of” means in front of or performing better than competitors.</b><br>Correct sentence: “We need to plan carefully to stay <b>ahead</b> of our competition.”<br>“For,” “in” and “beyond” do not form this standard phrase.<br>Careful planning helps maintain a competitive lead.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ahead.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000075063","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the correct definition of the word “protege”? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A mentor or advisor"},"2":{"en":"A young person under the guidance of an older, more experienced person"},"3":{"en":"A person who offers help or support"},"4":{"en":"A competitor or rival"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Protégé (शिष्य) = a person guided by an older or more experienced patron.</b><br>The mentor provides guidance, while the protégé receives it.<br>A helper or supporter describes a patron rather than a protégé.<br>A competitor or rival is unrelated to the relationship.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A young person under the guidance of an older, more experienced person.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000075064","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Ignaminious</b> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Honorable"},"2":{"en":"Shameful"},"3":{"en":"Disgraceful"},"4":{"en":"Infamous"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Ignominious (अपमानजनक) = deserving or causing public disgrace.</b><br><b>Honorable (सम्माननीय)</b> = deserving respect ✔<br><b>Shameful (लज्जाजनक)</b> = causing shame<br><b>Disgraceful (अपमानजनक)</b> = bringing dishonour<br><b>Infamous (कुख्यात)</b> = famous for something bad<br>More antonyms: reputable, respectable, esteemed.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Honorable.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000075065","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br>To kick against the pricks [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To act with excessive caution"},"2":{"en":"To challenge injustice successfully"},"3":{"en":"To resist futilely against authority"},"4":{"en":"To support power without question"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Kick against the pricks (व्यर्थ विरोध करना)</b><br>It means resist authority or circumstances in a way that only hurts oneself.<br>Example: “Arguing against the inevitable was like kicking against the pricks.”<br>Excessive caution and successful challenge are not implied; unquestioning support is the opposite.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): To resist futilely against authority.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000075066","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of “the process where particles form clumps or flocs”. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Flaculation"},"2":{"en":"Flocullation"},"3":{"en":"Flocculation"},"4":{"en":"Flokkulation"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Flocculation (गुच्छन) = the process by which particles form clumps or flocs.</b><br>The correct spelling has double “c” and a single “l.”<br><b>Flaculation</b> omits “cc” and uses “a”; <b>Flocullation</b> doubles “l” but has one “c.”<br><b>Flokkulation</b> wrongly uses “kk.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Flocculation.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000075067","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “Fear of the number thirteen”. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Triskaidekaphobia"},"2":{"en":"Hexakosioihexekontahexaphobia"},"3":{"en":"Pyrophobia"},"4":{"en":"Aichmophobia"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Triskaidekaphobia (संख्या 13 का भय) = fear of the number thirteen.</b><br><b>Hexakosioihexekontahexaphobia (666 का भय)</b> = fear of the number 666<br><b>Pyrophobia (आग का भय)</b> = fear of fire<br><b>Aichmophobia (नुकीली वस्तुओं का भय)</b> = fear of sharp objects<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Triskaidekaphobia.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000075068","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Select the correct option:<br>The grant allowed researchers to delve ___ topics previously considered fringe. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"onto"},"2":{"en":"into"},"3":{"en":"in"},"4":{"en":"about"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Delve into” means investigate or examine deeply.</b><br>Correct sentence: “The grant allowed researchers to delve <b>into</b> topics previously considered fringe.”<br>“Onto,” “in” and “about” do not form the standard phrasal verb.<br>The researchers investigate neglected subjects in depth.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): into.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000075069","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>The judge not only dismissed the petition (1)/ but also reprimanding the lawyer (2)/ for misrepresenting facts (3)/ during the cross-examination. (4) [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Not only … but also” must join parallel verb forms.</b><br>“Dismissed” is a finite past-tense verb, so part (2) should read “but also <b>reprimanded</b> the lawyer.”<br>“Reprimanding” breaks the parallelism.<br>The other parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (2).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000075070","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>While the director had hoped for clarity, (1)/ what emerged instead were overlapping interpretations (2)/ that undermined the coherence (3)/ of the original draft. (4) [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The subject “what emerged” is a singular nominal clause.</b><br>Part (2) should read “what emerged instead <b>was</b> overlapping interpretations.”<br>The complement may be plural, but the verb agrees with the singular what-clause.<br>The other parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (2).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000075071","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>Who wrote this poem? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"By whom was this poem written?"},"2":{"en":"By whom is this poem written?"},"3":{"en":"By whom has this poem been written?"},"4":{"en":"By whom was this poem being written?"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Who” becomes “by whom,” and simple past becomes “was/were + past participle.”</b><br>The singular poem takes “was written.”<br>B changes to simple present, C to present perfect, and D to past continuous.<br>The interrogative structure is retained.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): By whom was this poem written?.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000075072","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>The speaker's tone conveyed more than the actual words. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"More than the actual words were conveyed by the speaker's tone."},"2":{"en":"The speaker's tone has conveyed more than just words."},"3":{"en":"What was conveyed by the speaker was more than actual words."},"4":{"en":"The speaker's tone was conveyed more than the actual words."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The object phrase “more than the actual words” becomes the passive subject.</b><br>The agent remains “the speaker’s tone,” and the simple past becomes “were conveyed.”<br>B and C change the structure and agent; D wrongly retains the tone as subject.<br>A preserves the intended comparison.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): More than the actual words were conveyed by the speaker's tone..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000075073","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>The doctor said that no sooner had the treatment begun than the symptoms improved. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“No sooner had the treatment begun than the symptoms improved,” said the doctor."},"2":{"en":"“As soon as the treatment began, symptoms improved,” said the doctor."},"3":{"en":"“No sooner the treatment began, the symptoms improved,” said the doctor."},"4":{"en":"“The symptoms improved once treatment began,” said the doctor."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Retain the “No sooner … than” correlative structure in direct speech.</b><br>The inversion “had the treatment begun” is grammatically correct after “No sooner.”<br>B and D paraphrase the structure; C omits the auxiliary and uses “the” instead of “than.”<br>A preserves the exact wording and meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): “No sooner had the treatment begun than the symptoms improved,” said the doctor..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000075074","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate synonym of the underlined word.<br>The instructions were <u>ambiguous</u> and caused confusion. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Clear"},"2":{"en":"Certain"},"3":{"en":"Vague"},"4":{"en":"Exact"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Ambiguous (अस्पष्ट) = open to more than one interpretation.</b><br><b>Clear (स्पष्ट)</b> = easy to understand<br><b>Certain (निश्चित)</b> = definite<br><b>Vague (अस्पष्ट)</b> = unclear or imprecise ✔<br><b>Exact (यथार्थ)</b> = precise<br>More synonyms: equivocal, unclear, indeterminate.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Vague.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000075075","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"In the following question, the first and last parts of the sentence (1 and 6) are given. The rest of the sentence is split into four parts and named A, B, C, and D. These four parts are not given in their proper order. Read the sentence and find out which of the four combinations is correct.<br>1. Modern architects are increasingly<br>A. to combat rising pollution<br>B. designing vertical forests that<br>C. integrate lush vegetation into<br>D. high-rise residential buildings<br>6. and improve the local biodiversity. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ACDB"},"2":{"en":"BCDA"},"3":{"en":"DACB"},"4":{"en":"BADC"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: BCDA</b><br>B completes “are increasingly designing vertical forests that.”<br>C and D explain the design: vegetation integrated into high-rise buildings.<br>A introduces the environmental purpose and connects directly to part 6.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): BCDA.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000075076","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>As Dorothy and her companions approached the Emerald City, admiration was tempered by uneasiness. From afar, its towers gleamed like precious stones, creating an impression of extraordinary wealth. At the gate, however, every visitor was compelled to wear green spectacles. The Guardian claimed that the glasses protected the eyes from the city’s dazzling brilliance, but the travellers suspected a subtler purpose: the lenses might manipulate perception and make the city appear more magnificent than it actually was.<br><br>Within the walls, green dominated every aspect of life. Buildings seemed to be made of green marble, emeralds glittered on the walls, citizens wore green garments, and even the goods in the shops conformed to the same carefully maintained colour scheme. The uniformity suggested not merely decoration, but deliberate control over appearances.<br><br>Yet the splendour failed to quiet the travellers’ anxiety. Dorothy wished to return home, the Scarecrow sought intelligence, the Tin Woodman desired a heart, and the Lion longed for courage. Their private deficiencies mattered more than the city’s outward grandeur. Their hopes rested on the mysterious Wizard, although no citizen could clearly describe him. When informed that they would meet him separately, they felt increasingly vulnerable, for they had expected to draw courage from one another's presence.<br><br><br>What did the compulsory use of green spectacles lead the travellers to suspect? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The city was genuinely too bright for ordinary vision."},"2":{"en":"Visitors were required to follow local customs unquestioningly."},"3":{"en":"The Guardian intended to manipulate visitors’ perception of the city."},"4":{"en":"The Guardian wanted to distinguish citizens from outsiders."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Suspicion: The spectacles served perceptual manipulation rather than protection.</b><br><i>“The lenses might manipulate perception and make the city appear more magnificent than it actually was.”</i><br>This directly states their concern.<br>Genuine brightness, unquestioning custom and distinguishing outsiders are not their suspicion.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The Guardian intended to manipulate visitors’ perception of the city..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000075077","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>As Dorothy and her companions approached the Emerald City, admiration was tempered by uneasiness. From afar, its towers gleamed like precious stones, creating an impression of extraordinary wealth. At the gate, however, every visitor was compelled to wear green spectacles. The Guardian claimed that the glasses protected the eyes from the city’s dazzling brilliance, but the travellers suspected a subtler purpose: the lenses might manipulate perception and make the city appear more magnificent than it actually was.<br><br>Within the walls, green dominated every aspect of life. Buildings seemed to be made of green marble, emeralds glittered on the walls, citizens wore green garments, and even the goods in the shops conformed to the same carefully maintained colour scheme. The uniformity suggested not merely decoration, but deliberate control over appearances.<br><br>Yet the splendour failed to quiet the travellers’ anxiety. Dorothy wished to return home, the Scarecrow sought intelligence, the Tin Woodman desired a heart, and the Lion longed for courage. Their private deficiencies mattered more than the city’s outward grandeur. Their hopes rested on the mysterious Wizard, although no citizen could clearly describe him. When informed that they would meet him separately, they felt increasingly vulnerable, for they had expected to draw courage from one another's presence.<br><br><br>The phrase “admiration was tempered by uneasiness” means that the travellers’ admiration was: [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"completely replaced by fear."},"2":{"en":"reduced or restrained by anxiety."},"3":{"en":"strengthened by uncertainty."},"4":{"en":"concealed from the citizens."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Tempered (संतुलित या कम किया गया) = moderated or restrained.</b><br>The travellers admired the city, but uneasiness limited that admiration.<br>The fear did not completely replace or strengthen admiration.<br>No concealment from citizens is stated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): reduced or restrained by anxiety..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000075078","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>As Dorothy and her companions approached the Emerald City, admiration was tempered by uneasiness. From afar, its towers gleamed like precious stones, creating an impression of extraordinary wealth. At the gate, however, every visitor was compelled to wear green spectacles. The Guardian claimed that the glasses protected the eyes from the city’s dazzling brilliance, but the travellers suspected a subtler purpose: the lenses might manipulate perception and make the city appear more magnificent than it actually was.<br><br>Within the walls, green dominated every aspect of life. Buildings seemed to be made of green marble, emeralds glittered on the walls, citizens wore green garments, and even the goods in the shops conformed to the same carefully maintained colour scheme. The uniformity suggested not merely decoration, but deliberate control over appearances.<br><br>Yet the splendour failed to quiet the travellers’ anxiety. Dorothy wished to return home, the Scarecrow sought intelligence, the Tin Woodman desired a heart, and the Lion longed for courage. Their private deficiencies mattered more than the city’s outward grandeur. Their hopes rested on the mysterious Wizard, although no citizen could clearly describe him. When informed that they would meet him separately, they felt increasingly vulnerable, for they had expected to draw courage from one another's presence.<br><br><br>What can be inferred from the uniform use of green throughout the city? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Other colours were unavailable to the citizens."},"2":{"en":"The city depended mainly on the emerald trade."},"3":{"en":"The city promoted individuality among its citizens."},"4":{"en":"The uniformity suggested deliberate control over appearances."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Inference: The colour scheme is an instrument of appearance management.</b><br><i>“The uniformity suggested not merely decoration, but deliberate control over appearances.”</i><br>Scarcity of colours and an emerald-based economy are not stated.<br>Uniformity discourages rather than promotes individuality.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The uniformity suggested deliberate control over appearances..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000075079","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>As Dorothy and her companions approached the Emerald City, admiration was tempered by uneasiness. From afar, its towers gleamed like precious stones, creating an impression of extraordinary wealth. At the gate, however, every visitor was compelled to wear green spectacles. The Guardian claimed that the glasses protected the eyes from the city’s dazzling brilliance, but the travellers suspected a subtler purpose: the lenses might manipulate perception and make the city appear more magnificent than it actually was.<br><br>Within the walls, green dominated every aspect of life. Buildings seemed to be made of green marble, emeralds glittered on the walls, citizens wore green garments, and even the goods in the shops conformed to the same carefully maintained colour scheme. The uniformity suggested not merely decoration, but deliberate control over appearances.<br><br>Yet the splendour failed to quiet the travellers’ anxiety. Dorothy wished to return home, the Scarecrow sought intelligence, the Tin Woodman desired a heart, and the Lion longed for courage. Their private deficiencies mattered more than the city’s outward grandeur. Their hopes rested on the mysterious Wizard, although no citizen could clearly describe him. When informed that they would meet him separately, they felt increasingly vulnerable, for they had expected to draw courage from one another's presence.<br><br><br>Why did the travellers feel vulnerable when asked to meet the Wizard separately? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They believed that the Wizard would reject individual requests."},"2":{"en":"They feared that the Guardian had deceived them."},"3":{"en":"They would lose the emotional support of their companions."},"4":{"en":"They had forgotten how to explain their personal needs."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Reason: Separation removed their shared source of courage.</b><br><i>“They had expected to draw courage from one another's presence.”</i><br>Meeting separately therefore deprived them of companions’ emotional support.<br>Rejection, Guardian deception and forgotten requests are not stated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): They would lose the emotional support of their companions..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000075080","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>As Dorothy and her companions approached the Emerald City, admiration was tempered by uneasiness. From afar, its towers gleamed like precious stones, creating an impression of extraordinary wealth. At the gate, however, every visitor was compelled to wear green spectacles. The Guardian claimed that the glasses protected the eyes from the city’s dazzling brilliance, but the travellers suspected a subtler purpose: the lenses might manipulate perception and make the city appear more magnificent than it actually was.<br><br>Within the walls, green dominated every aspect of life. Buildings seemed to be made of green marble, emeralds glittered on the walls, citizens wore green garments, and even the goods in the shops conformed to the same carefully maintained colour scheme. The uniformity suggested not merely decoration, but deliberate control over appearances.<br><br>Yet the splendour failed to quiet the travellers’ anxiety. Dorothy wished to return home, the Scarecrow sought intelligence, the Tin Woodman desired a heart, and the Lion longed for courage. Their private deficiencies mattered more than the city’s outward grandeur. Their hopes rested on the mysterious Wizard, although no citizen could clearly describe him. When informed that they would meet him separately, they felt increasingly vulnerable, for they had expected to draw courage from one another's presence.<br><br><br>Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"External magnificence may conceal uncertainty and manipulation."},"2":{"en":"Friendship is valuable only in dangerous situations."},"3":{"en":"Personal desires prevent people from appreciating beauty."},"4":{"en":"Wealth and authority always produce fear among visitors."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Central idea: Splendour does not guarantee truth, security or happiness.</b><br>The green spectacles suggest manipulated magnificence, while the travellers remain anxious and focused on private needs.<br>Friendship is not limited to danger, and desires do not erase appreciation of beauty.<br>The passage does not claim wealth and authority always cause fear.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): External magnificence may conceal uncertainty and manipulation..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};